('Andrew Felbinger','Principal','Urban Innovation Fund','{}','{}',array['Pre-seed','Seed','Series A']::text[],true,null,null,array['US/Canada']::text[],'https://twitter.com/a_felbinger','https://www.linkedin.com/in/andrew-felbinger-22687813/','Andrew is a Principal at the Urban Innovation Fund, a venture capital firm investing in entrepreneurs shaping the future of cities. The fund provides seed capital and regulatory support to entrepreneurs solving our toughest urban challenges – helping them grow into tomorrow’s most valued companies. Prior to joining the Urban Innovation Fund, Andrew received his MBA at the Wharton School of Business in 2018 and graduated as the Valedictorian at Seton Hall University with a cumulative GPA of 4.0 in 2012. His previous work experience includes working for Barclays in their Global Capital Markets Division and Castellan Real Estate Partners on their Acquisition Team.','Minneapolis, Minnesota','2023-04-17T19:31:17.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Andrew Firlik','Managing Partner','Jazz Venture Partners',array['$0 - $100K','$100K - $500K','$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M']::text[],array['Enterprise','BioTech','Digital Health','AI','Developer Tools','AR/VR','Gaming/eSports']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Series B+']::text[],true,null,null,array['US/Canada']::text[],'https://twitter.com/andrewfirlik','https://www.linkedin.com/in/andrew-firlik-b97a0977/','Andrew has experience in venture capital, company building, technology development, and neurosurgery. He has served as founder, investor, director, and chairman of many successful companies. Previously, he was a partner at Flare Capital Partners (formerly known as Foundation Medical Partners) and a principal at Canaan Partners. He was a founder and invented the core technology of Northstar Neuroscience, which went public and was subsequently acquired by St. Jude Medical. He also served as chairman of IntElect Medical, which was acquired by Boston Scientific. Andrew''s investments prior to JAZZ include BridgePoint Medical (acquired by Boston Scientific), Explorys (acquired by IBM), Functional Neuromodulation, and Visiogen (acquired by Abbott). Prior to venture capital, Andrew was a board-certified neurosurgeon and served as clinical assistant professor of neurosurgery at Yale School of Medicine and New York University School of Medicine.','San Francisco, California','2023-04-21T05:38:30.000Z'::timestamptz),
