('Arianna Simpson','General Partner','Andreessen Horowitz',array['$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M','$10M - $50M','$50M+']::text[],array['BioTech','CleanTech/Environment','Enterprise','FinTech','Marketplaces','Retail','SaaS','Sales & CRM','Crypto/Blockchain','AI','Developer Tools','Cybersecurity','Web3','DeepTech','Digital Health','Consumer','AR/VR','Gaming/eSports']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Series B+']::text[],true,'Freedom Robotics; Celo',null,array['Asia-Pacific','US/Canada']::text[],'https://twitter.com/ariannasimpson','https://www.linkedin.com/in/ariannasimpson/','Arianna previously founded Autonomous Partners, an investment fund focused on cryptocurrencies and digital assets. She also helped launch Crystal Towers Capital, an early-stage fund investing primarily in YC companies, in 2015. Arianna previously spent time working in sales and product roles at Facebook and BitGo, an enterprise security company for bitcoin and other digital currencies.','New York, New York','2023-04-21T05:38:30.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Ariel Sterman','Vice President','Bessemer Venture Partners',array['$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M','$10M - $50M','$50M+']::text[],array['AI','Developer Tools','BioTech','Digital Health','Consumer','FinTech']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Series B+']::text[],true,null,null,array['US/Canada','Israel','Asia-Pacific','Europe']::text[],'https://twitter.com/ArielSterman','https://www.linkedin.com/in/sterman/','Ariel is a vice president in Bessemer’s Israel office where he focuses on companies in Israel and Europe. He was featured on Forbes 30 Under 30 for Israel. Prior to joining Bessemer, Ariel spent several years at Stripes Group, a growth equity firm in NYC, where he spearheaded the firm’s Israeli sourcing efforts and drove its first investment in the geography (Monday.com’s $50M Series C). He also played an active role in supporting companies across the firm’s consumer internet, fintech, and SaaS portfolio.','Israel','2023-04-20T23:03:06.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Arielle Zuckerberg','General Partner','Long Journey Ventures; Humin',array['$100K - $500K','$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M','$0 - $100K']::text[],array['Consumer Health','FinTech','Food and Beverage','Future of Work','Marketplaces','Media/Content','Parenting/Families','Consumer']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Pre-seed']::text[],true,'Mason; The Ticket Fairy; Juni Learning; Partender; Tiny Farms; Futurefly','a.zuckerberg@kpcb.com',array['US/Canada']::text[],'https://twitter.com/ariellezuck?lang=en','https://www.linkedin.com/in/ariellezuckerberg/','My background is in product management so I love to jam and brainstorm, but what underpins how I work with founders is authentic human connection, empathy, and trust. I believe that a big part of my role as a VC is to help remove barriers, open doors, and be a trusted partner throughout this incredible journey. Before joining LJV, I was at Coatue, where I helped build the strategy for our first early stage fund and get it off the ground. I’m also the co-founder of Lej, a clothing brand, as well as a part-time DJ.','San Francisco, California','2023-04-12T19:30:01.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Arjan Schütte','Founder & Managing Partner','Core Innovation Capital',array['$100K - $500K','$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M']::text[],array['FinTech','Web3']::text[],array['Pre-seed','Seed','Series A']::text[],true,'SynapseFi','arjan@corevc.com',array['US/Canada']::text[],'https://twitter.com/arjanschutte','https://www.linkedin.com/in/arjanschutte/','Arjan [pronounced ARE-yawn] is a trusted and experienced venture investor and founder of Core Innovation Capital, a leading venture capital fund investing in financial services companies that democratize prosperity. He is a passionate advocate for market-based financial access and empowerment. Arjan writes regularly, and has been noted in the Wall Street Journal, New York Times, and Economist, and in the documentary, Spent. He speaks regularly including at the White House, SXSW, Stanford, Harvard, and MIT. On a local level he serves on the Compton Community Development Corporation Board. Prior, he spent a decade as an operator in several venture backed startups as a technology leader, product- and general manager including Pierian Spring Software, Cognitive Concepts (acquired by Houghton Mifflin), Capella Learning (now NASDAQ: CPLA), and DoTheGood.','Los Angeles, California','2023-05-05T16:13:02.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Arjun Chopra','Partner','Floodgate
