('Bhaskar “BG” Ghosh','CTO','8VC',array['$100K - $500K','$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M','$10M - $50M']::text[],array['AI','Developer Tools','Logistics','DeepTech','BioTech','Digital Health','Defense, Gov, & Legal','FinTech','B2C/E-Commerce','Enterprise','Generalist']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Pre-seed','Series B+']::text[],true,'Instawork',null,array['US/Canada']::text[],'https://twitter.com/bgmusings','https://www.linkedin.com/in/ghoshbhaskar/','Bhaskar “BG” Ghosh is the CTO at 8VC, having initially joined the company as an Advisor in December 2015. Since receiving his PhD in Computer Science from Yale, BG has had a distinguished career in Silicon Valley, working for 20+ years in technology leadership in diverse domains including enterprise data and web infrastructure, digital advertising, social networks, and consumer fintech. Previously, he ran technology at Nerdwallet as VP of Engineering, helped build the teams and back-ends that helped fuel LinkedIn’s meteoric growth as its Head of Data Engineering, and led engineering for the pioneering Yahoo! Right Media Display Advertising Exchange. BG built his deep technology and data chops developing RDMBS kernels at top enterprise data-platform companies like Oracle and Informix. At 8VC, BG works with the entrepreneurs and leaders in our portfolio as a virtual CTO, and in finding the next big investment idea across technology domains.','Palo Alto, California','2023-04-20T23:35:58.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Bijan Sabet','General Partner','Spark Capital',array['$100K - $500K','$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M','$10M - $50M','$0 - $100K']::text[],array['Enterprise','Media/Content','Social Networks','DeepTech','Consumer','AI','Developer Tools','Marketplaces','FinTech','Web3']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Series B+']::text[],true,'Beam; Stack Overflow; TEOOH; Slite; Overtime; Foursquare; Lily; Hello Alfred; Twitter; Tumblr Inc.',null,array['US/Canada']::text[],'https://twitter.com/bijan','https://www.linkedin.com/in/bijansabet/','Cofounder and General Partner at Spark Capital. Spark currently manages over $4B across venture and venture growth funds. Led our investment in Twitter (NYSE: TWTR) in early 2008 and served on their board from 2008-2011. Also led the seed investment in Tumblr (acquired by Yahoo!) and served on their board of directors for the entire duration of the company. Other investments include: Stack Overflow (acquired by Prosus N.V.), Overtime, Crowdrise (acquired by GoFundMe), Trello (acquired by Atlassian), Sincerely (acquired by Liberty Interactive Corporation), RunKeeper (acquires by ASICS), Foursquare, Boxee (acquired by Samsung), OMGPOP (acquired by Zynga) and thePlatform (acquired by Comcast).','Boston, Massachusetts','2023-04-21T00:16:39.000Z'::timestamptz),
