('Bruce Barron','Founding Partner','Origin Ventures',array['$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M']::text[],array['Enterprise','B2C/E-Commerce','Future of Work','Marketplaces']::text[],array['Seed','Series A']::text[],true,null,null,'{}','https://twitter.com/brucenbarron','https://www.linkedin.com/in/bruce-barron-2711741/','serves on the boards of the American Cancer Society, the Chicago Baseball Cancer Charities, and Israel Cancer Research Fund (ICRF) Chicago and International Chapters. provides funding for the Origin Ventures Academy for Entrepreneurial Leadership at the University of Illinois and the Jacki & Bruce Barron Cancer Research Scholars Program, a collaboration between ICRF and City of Hope. named a Crain’s Chicago Business Tech 50 member in 2013','Chicago, Illinois','2023-04-21T00:16:39.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Bruce Dunlevie','General Partner','Benchmark Capital',array['$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M','$10M - $50M','$500K - $1M']::text[],array['Cloud Infrastructure','Enterprise','Local Services','Social Commerce','Social Networks','AI','Developer Tools','Marketplaces','Consumer']::text[],array['Seed','Series B+','Series A']::text[],true,'Mon Ami; Euclid; Aquifi; The We Company; Marin Software; Klip; Tabula; Wealthfront',null,array['US/Canada']::text[],null,'https://www.linkedin.com/in/bruce-dunlevie-4285603/','Bruce Dunlevie is the General Partner at Benchmark. Additionally, Bruce Dunlevie has had 5 past jobs including Systems Designer & Programmer at Accenture. Bruce previously served as a member of the board of directors of Rambus Inc., a technology licensing company, from March 1990 to June 2011, and as a member of the board of directors of Palm,Inc., a provider of mobile products, from October 2003 to October 2007. Bruce holds a B.A. in History and English from Rice University and an M.B.A. from the Stanford Graduate School of Business.','Atherton, California','2023-04-21T00:16:39.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Bruce Hamilton','General Partner','Mech Ventures',array['$100K - $500K']::text[],array['AR/VR','Consumer','Crypto/Blockchain','B2C/E-Commerce','Entertainment','Future of Work','IoT','Media','B2B SaaS','Social Media','Marketplaces','FinTech','Gaming/eSports','Direct-to-Consumer (DTC)']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Pre-seed']::text[],false,'CrwdBoost; Wing Zero Apps','bruce@mech.ventures',array['Global']::text[],null,'https://www.linkedin.com/in/ibrucehamilton/','Bruce Hamilton is a General Partner at Mech Ventures, a venture capital firm for pop culture, and the Founder / CEO of Wing Zero Apps (formerly known as Doly). He is passionate about using his entrepreneur experience, aesthetics, marketing and creative background to develop numerous brands (Wing Zero Apps, CrwdBoost, Grey Label Co.) and help them scale. Bruce previously served as the Chief Marketing Officer at House of Glue, an art e-commerce brand. Prior to his founding Wing Zero Apps, he was the Founder & CEO of Samurai Entertainment, a talent management firm representing artists, producers and songwriters. Bruce also worked at Epic Records as an A&R where he worked with artists such as Travis Scott, Fifth Harmony, and several others.','Los Angeles Metropolitan','2023-04-29T10:25:19.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Bryan Cressey','Co-Founder and Senior Advisor','Frist Cressey Ventures','{}',array['Digital Health']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Series B+']::text[],true,null,null,array['US/Canada']::text[],'https://twitter.com/BryanCCressey','https://www.linkedin.com/in/bryan-cressey/','Bryan Cressey is a pioneer in the field of private equity investing and co-founder of three of the largest private equity firms in the US. He has managed billions of dollars of private capital, spent his career investing in healthcare, is a co-founder of FCV and serves as a Senior Advisor to the firm. He is an acknowledged expert in healthcare, where he has invested over 30 years, and his firms are well known for their consistently strong investment returns. He has been featured in Time Magazine and Fortune Magazine and is asked to speak nationwide on healthcare and private equity investing. He served as Chairman of an NYSE company, Belden, and is a Director of several others, and has been elected to Chicago’s Entrepreneurial Hall of Fame and Chicago’s Business Hall of Fame. Bryan recently created an addiction treatment center called Above and Beyond, on Chicago’s Westside, providing life transformation opportunities, free to the homeless and poor.','Chicago, Illinois','2023-04-19T19:08:20.000Z'::timestamptz),
