('Byron Deeter','Partner','Bessemer Venture Partners',array['$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M','$10M - $50M']::text[],array['Cloud Infrastructure','SaaS','Social Networks','AI','Developer Tools','Cybersecurity','BioTech','Digital Health','Consumer','FinTech']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Series B+']::text[],true,'ScaleFactor; ServiceTitan; Zylo; Rainforest QA; Glint; Guild Education; Tile; Gainsight; Twilio; Box; Canva; LaunchDarkly; Yotpo','byron@bvp.com',array['USA','Canada','Israel','Asia-Pacific','Europe','US/Canada']::text[],'https://twitter.com/bdeeter','https://www.linkedin.com/in/byrondeeter/','To date, nineteen of Byron’s investments are valued above $1 billion, including ten IPOs and counting. Byron first raised a Series A with Bessemer Venture Partners back in 2000, as CEO and founder of Trigo Technologies. His company grew to be one of the first global SaaS companies, reaching profitability and was successfully sold to IBM. Byron foresaw that cloud computing would not only change the way people built new technologies but also how The Cloud would systematically run the world. In 2005, Byron returned to Bessemer, this time to lead the fund’s global cloud practice. He graduated with honors from The University of California, Berkeley.','Atherton, California','2023-04-20T23:03:06.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Byron Ling','Partner','Twelve Below',array['$100K - $500K','$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M','$10M - $50M']::text[],array['Enterprise','Health & Hospital Services','Health IT','Consumer','FinTech','Digital Health','B2C/E-Commerce','EdTech','Climate','Future of Work']::text[],array['Pre-seed','Seed']::text[],true,null,'byron@twelvebelow.co',array['US/Canada']::text[],'https://twitter.com/byronling1?lang=en','https://www.linkedin.com/in/byron-ling-10b7474/','looks for founders with unique insights about attractive markets.  have been an early-stage investor for the last seven years in NYC, most recently as a Partner at Canaan where they led investments in software and health care companies such as Ro, Papa, Italic and others. was a Principal at Primary Venture Partners on the firm’s inaugural seed fund was an operator with Gilt Groupe as one of the earliest employees at the Series A started their career in investment banking at a firm called Sagent Advisors','New York, New York','2023-04-20T23:35:58.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Calvin Chin','Angel Investor','The E14 Fund',array['$100K - $500K','$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M']::text[],array['Hardware','Media','AI','Developer Tools','FinTech','Food & Ag','Future of Work','Digital Health','Logistics','Climate','BioTech']::text[],array['Seed','Pre-seed','Series A']::text[],true,'Pi Charging; Pienso; Ligandal; Wise Systems; Enigma; ThruWave; Kiwi Technologies; Culture Robotics','calvin@transi.st',array['US/Canada']::text[],'https://twitter.com/c10n?lang=en','https://www.linkedin.com/in/calvinwuchin','Previously he was co-founder CEO of Transist, an incubator and investor in impact-driven tech startups in China and the US. Earlier Calvin was founder CEO of Qifang, China''s first online student loan service and the first Chinese company recognized by the World Economic Forum as a Technology Pioneer. Calvin is a member of the Aspen Institute''s inaugural China Fellowship Program, a WEF Young Global Leader. He was named one of Fast Company magazine''s 100 Most Creative People In Business for 2011, was named 2009 Chinese Business Leader of the Year by Horasis and Baker & McKenzie, and is a Social Innovation Park Fellow. He has an MBA from TRIUM (NYU, LSE, HEC Paris), a B.A. from Yale University and has also studied social entrepreneurship, global leadership and other management and policy subjects at Harvard University and INSEAD.','San Francisco, California','2023-04-20T23:03:06.000Z'::timestamptz),
