('Camila Saruhashi','Principal','QED Investors',array['$500K - $1M']::text[],array['Crypto/Blockchain','InsureTech','Proptech','FinTech']::text[],array['Pre-seed','Seed','Series A']::text[],false,'Capchase',null,array['Latin America','US/Canada']::text[],null,'https://www.linkedin.com/in/camilakey','Camila is a Principal at QED Investors, a global venture capital firm specialized in fintech companies ($3B+ AUM, 150+ companies, 20+ unicorns, 13 countries). She is based in San Francisco and focuses on early stage (pre-seed, seed and Series A) investments. Prior to QED, she spent her career in fintech as an operator in fast growing companies such as Nubank and Earnin, working in key leadership roles from head of operations to product.','San Francisco Bay Area','2023-04-20T23:03:06.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Carmen Chang','General Partner and Head of Asia','New Enterprise Associates',array['$100K - $500K','$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M','$10M - $50M']::text[],array['Health IT','Consumer','BioTech','Cybersecurity','Digital Health']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Series B+']::text[],true,'Drive.ai; Testlio; Alien Technology; Cloudflare; Coursera',null,array['US/Canada']::text[],null,'https://www.linkedin.com/in/carmen-chang-94222211/','focused on building NEA''s global organization and portfolio in China and other emerging markets in Asia but still invests in the US and Europe. Prior to joining NEA, Carmen was a partner at a major Silicon Valley law firm, where she specialized in corporate and securities law and led that firm''s China practice.','Palo Alto, California','2023-04-19T20:16:24.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Carmen Yuen','General Partner','Vertex Ventures',array['$100K - $500K','$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M','$0 - $100K']::text[],array['Enterprise']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Series B+']::text[],true,null,null,array['US/Canada','Asia-Pacific','Israel','India']::text[],null,'https://www.linkedin.com/in/YuenCarmen','Carmen Yuen joined Vertex Ventures Singapore office in 2014. Her focus is in Singapore and Southeast Asia. Carmen has served many years in Singapore’s government-backed venture capital initiatives including EDB Investments and Spring SEEDS Capital where she worked closely with many start-up companies in Singapore. Prior to joining Vertex, she was with Majuven, a Singapore angel fund. Carmen currently serves on the Board of TickledMedia (dba TheAsianParent.com).','Singapore','2023-04-19T20:19:33.000Z'::timestamptz);

