('Caroline Brown','Managing Director','Closed Loop Partners',array['$0 - $100K','$100K - $500K','$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M']::text[],array['Climate','BioTech','Logistics','CPG/D2C','Food & Ag']::text[],array['Pre-seed','Seed']::text[],true,null,null,array['US/Canada','Africa','Latin America','India','Asia-Pacific','Europe','Israel','Australia/New Zealand','Middle East','North Africa']::text[],null,'https://www.linkedin.com/in/caroline-brown-12118495/','co-leads the growth equity investment practice which includes circular solutions for fashion, material innovation, supply chain technology, food & agriculture. Prior to joining CLP, she was CEO of Donna Karan International (DKI) and DKNY was CEO of Akris, Inc., the Swiss based luxury brand  began her career at Giorgio Armani with over a decade in leadership roles of Marketing & Communications. an advisor for the Martin Trust Center for MIT Entrepreneurship at MIT Sloan School of Management, a member of the Board of Trustees for Choate Rosemary Hall and a member of the Women’s Forum of New York','New York, New York','2023-04-19T20:26:44.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Caroline Weintraub','Senior Associate','True Beauty Ventures',array['$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M']::text[],array['Consumer']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Series B+']::text[],false,'AQUIS/K18; Crown Affair; Feals; Kinship; Maude','caroline@truebeautyventures.com',array['US/Canada']::text[],null,'https://www.linkedin.com/in/caroline-weintraub-b8ab6929/','Caroline is a Senior Associate at True Beauty Ventures and a recent graduate of Columbia Business School. At Columbia Business School, she was the co-president of the venture capital club and held various internships in consumer venture capital and high growth beauty start-ups. Prior to receiving her MBA, Caroline spent 4 years at Accenture as a management consultant. While at Accenture, Caroline assisted prestige beauty brands in a variety of strategy and operations projects, including new product launch improvements, effective risk management, and sales and operations planning. Caroline graduated magna cum laude from Northwestern University in 2015 with a degree in Journalism and received her MBA from Columbia Business School in 2021.','New York, New York','2023-02-24T12:21:12.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Carter Reum','Co-Founder and Partner','M13',array['$100K - $500K','$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M']::text[],array['Commercial Services','SMB Software','Consumer','Future of Work','Digital Health','B2C/E-Commerce','Marketplaces','FinTech','Proptech','Web3']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Pre-seed','Series B+']::text[],true,'Matterport; Social Native','carter@m13.co',array['US/Canada']::text[],null,'https://www.linkedin.com/in/carterreum/','Carter co-founded M13 in 2016 with his brother Courtney. The duo co-founded and sold VEEV, the spirits brand, and co-authored the bestseller “Shortcut Your Startup.” A former Goldman Sachs investment banker, Carter is a LACMA board member.','Los Angeles, California','2023-04-21T00:16:39.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Casey Aylward','Partner','Accel',array['$100K - $500K','$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M']::text[],array['Consumer','SMB Software','Generalist','AI','Developer Tools','Cybersecurity','Enterprise','FinTech','Digital Health','B2C/E-Commerce']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Series B+']::text[],true,null,null,array['US/Canada','Africa','Latin America','India','Asia-Pacific','Europe','Israel','Australia/New Zealand','Middle East','North Africa']::text[],'https://twitter.com/caseyaylward','https://www.linkedin.com/in/caseyaylward/','Casey joined Accel in 2022. Prior to joining Accel, Casey worked at Costanoa Ventures, an early-stage enterprise fund, where she led and incubated several investments in developer tools, data infrastructure, and security. Before investing, Casey was a software engineer at Pinterest where she worked on commerce, collaboration, and core products. Casey joined Pinterest via an acquisition of a former Accel portfolio company, URX, where she was also a software engineer.','San Francisco, California','2023-04-20T23:35:58.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Casper de Clercq','General Partner','Norwest Venture Partners',array['$0 - $25K','$25K - $100K']::text[],array['Consumer Health','Health & Hospital Services','Health IT','Pharmaceuticals','Enterprise','B2C/E-Commerce','FinTech','AI','Developer Tools','EdTech','Proptech','Future of Work']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Series B+']::text[],true,'Monogram Health; Clever Care Health Plan Inc.; Robin Healthcare; Misfit Wearables; Telcare; iRhythm Technologies; BASIS Science; AtheroMed',null,array['India','US/Canada','Latin America']::text[],'https://www.twitter.com/Casper_deClercq','https://www.linkedin.com/in/casper-de-clercq-8a746/','With over 30 years of experience, Casper is a veteran of the medical device and life sciences industry, having led marketing and commercialization efforts for companies that span the healthcare space. He brings extensive operating knowledge to Norwest Venture Partners, where he focuses on mid-to-late-stage investments in consumer and digital health, healthcare IT, medical devices and diagnostics, technology-enabled healthcare services, and specialty pharmaceuticals.','San Francisco, California','2023-04-20T23:35:58.000Z'::timestamptz),
