('Cat Hernandez','General Partner','The Venture Collective (TVC)',array['$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M']::text[],array['Climate','Consumer','B2C/E-Commerce','Education','Future of Work','Health and Wellness','Healthcare/Medtech','IoT','Life Sciences','Productivity','B2B SaaS','Social Media','SaaS','BioTech','Marketplaces','FinTech']::text[],array['Seed','Pre-seed']::text[],false,'Jefa; Knoma; SimpliFed; Upside; Violet','cat@theventurecollective.com',array['Europe','Latin America','US/Canada']::text[],'https://twitter.com/catmhernandez','https://www.linkedin.com/in/catmhernandez/','Cat spent a decade operating in early stage startups before joining the Primary Ventures partnership where she played a critical role in shaping the firm''s post-investment approach for the better part of five years. Today, she is a General Partner and founding team member at The Venture Collective (TVC), a transformational, early stage venture business that is on a mission to bridge the funding gap for underrepresented founders on their path to building category-defining, purpose driven companies.','New York, New York','2023-04-21T00:16:39.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Catherine Wu','Partner','Index Ventures',array['$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M','$10M - $50M']::text[],array['AI','Developer Tools','Cybersecurity','BioTech','Consumer']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Series B+']::text[],true,null,null,array['US/Canada','Europe','Israel']::text[],'https://twitter.com/_catherinewu','https://www.linkedin.com/in/cat-wu/','Cat focuses on early-stage investments in enterprise software. She’s particularly interested in data infrastructure, developer tools, and artificial intelligence. Prior to joining Index, Cat worked at Elementl, maker of the open-source data orchestrator Dagster. There, she led the development of the commercial product, Dagster Cloud. Previously, Cat was an early engineer at Scale, where she grew the labeler community and partnered with strategic AV customers. Before that, she worked at Yelp, JPMorgan and YouTube. Cat graduated from Princeton University with a BSE in Computer Science. She currently lives in San Francisco and is an avid reader, occasional cook, and constant tinkerer.','San Francisco, California','2023-04-18T20:07:43.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Chad Byers','Co-Founder and General Partner','Susa Ventures',array['$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M','$500K - $1M']::text[],array['Cloud','Enterprise','Healthcare/Medtech','Industrial','InsureTech','Proptech','B2B SaaS','Supply Chain','Real Estate','SaaS','Marketplaces','FinTech','Logistics','Digital Health','Consumer','DeepTech']::text[],array['Pre-seed','Seed','Series B+','Series A']::text[],true,'Andela; Mux; Newfront Insurance; Robinhood; Stord; Sundae; Viz.ai; Policygenius; Naborly; WorkRamp; Troops.ai; Locale; Spring Discovery; Sell with AMI; Carta; Whisper','chad@susaventures.com',array['Africa','Oceania','Europe','Latin America','US/Canada','India']::text[],'https://twitter.com/chadbyers','https://www.linkedin.com/in/chadabyers/','Chad is a co-founder and General Partner at Susa Ventures. He focused on investments in fintech, healthcare and logistics. He led or co-led Susa''s investments in: Robinhood (fintech, seed); now public $HOOD, Andela (recruiting tech, seed); now Series E @ $1.6B, Mux (SaaS, seed); now Series D @ $1.6B, Stord (supply chain, seed); now Series D @ $1.1B, Newfront Insurance (fintech, seed); now Series C @ $1B+, Viz.ai (healthcare, seed); now Series C @ $600m+, Sundae (property tech, seed); now Series C @ $600m+. In his free time, he loves skiing, any and all team sports, video games, and musicals. Focuses on investments in marketplaces, fintech, and healthcare. Led Susa''s investments in Robinhood, Andela, Newfront Insurance and Stord. Prior to Susa Ventures, Chad was the senior director of platform at Integrate.com and held various marketing and product roles at Silver Spring Networks, Bloom Energy, and Electronic Arts.','San Francisco, California','2023-04-21T00:16:39.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Chad Packard','Partner','Pelion Venture Partners',array['$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M']::text[],array['Media','Cybersecurity']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Series B+']::text[],true,null,'chad@pelionvp.com',array['US/Canada']::text[],null,'https://www.linkedin.com/in/chad-packard-2397022/','Chad Packard joined Pelion Venture Partners in 2008. Prior to Pelion, he was a Director of Cougar Capital, a venture fund managed by Brigham Young University. He is a member of the state bar association of California.','Salt Lake City, Utah','2023-04-19T20:53:44.000Z'::timestamptz),
