('Chang Xu','Partner','Basis Set Ventures',array['$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M']::text[],array['AI','Analytics','API','Automation','Cloud','Crypto/Blockchain','DeepTech','Developer Tools','Enterprise','IoT','Productivity','Proptech','B2B SaaS','Cloud Infrastructure','Future of Work','FinTech']::text[],array['Seed','Pre-seed','Series A']::text[],true,'Clutch; Octane; Orchest; Workstream','chang@basisset.com',array['Global','US/Canada','Asia-Pacific']::text[],'https://twitter.com/_changxu','https://www.linkedin.com/in/changx/','Chang previously was a Principal at Upfront Ventures, where she focused on investing in AI and the future of work. Prior to joining venture, she was a founder and operator. She was the first Product Manager at the Minerva Project and co-founded Onion Math, an ed-tech startup in China that has raised $90M. She started her career at BCG, advising clients across tech, retail, healthcare and private equity. She holds an MBA and AB in Applied Math and Computer Science from Harvard.','Los Angeles, California','2023-04-20T23:03:06.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Charles Beeler','Managing Director','Rally Ventures; El Dorado Ventures',array['$100K - $500K','$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M','$0 - $100K']::text[],array['Enterprise','Future of Work','Cybersecurity']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Series B+']::text[],true,null,'charles@eldorado.com',array['US/Canada']::text[],'https://twitter.com/charlesbeeler','https://www.linkedin.com/in/charlesbeeler/','Charles has been a venture capitalist since 1997 and has focused on early-stage business technology companies throughout his career. Charles co-founded Rally Ventures in 2012 with Jeff Hinck. He started his venture career as an associate at Scripps Ventures after working as an analyst at Piper Jaffray and earlier as a systems consultant at the Mayo Clinic, where he helped design a radiology information system. Some of Charles’ notable investments include: Coupa Software, which had a highly successful IPO in 2016 (Nasdaq: COUP); Compellent Technologies, which held an IPO and was subsequently sold to Dell, returning more than 9x invested capital; NuSpeed, which was acquired by Cisco Systems returning 55x invested capital; Verodin; and Twistlock.','Menlo Park, California','2023-04-20T01:26:37.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Charles Birnbaum','Partner','Bessemer Venture Partners',array['$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M','$10M - $50M','$50M+']::text[],array['Education','FinTech','Consumer','AI','Developer Tools','Cybersecurity','BioTech','Digital Health']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Series B+']::text[],true,'Carefull; Brightwheel; Fabric Technologies; Alloy; Shift Technology; Bread; Spruce Holdings; Betterment',null,array['US/Canada','Israel','Asia-Pacific','Europe']::text[],'https://twitter.com/cbirn','https://www.linkedin.com/in/charlesbirnbaum/','Charles Birnbaum is a partner in Bessemer’s New York office, where he invests in early-stage and promising companies in the U.S. and Europe. He has a strong interest in fintech infrastructure, embedded financial services, consumer-facing products, the powerful emergence of DeFi, and the consumer-facing companies and infrastructure players that will serve as a bridge between DeFi and TradFi. Before joining Bessemer in 2013, Charles was one of the earliest team members at Foursquare, the location-based mobile application and social network, where he helped to bring forth the company’s first merchant-facing tools.','New York, New York','2023-04-12T20:10:23.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Charles D. King','Co-Founder & Special General Partner','MaC VC; MaC Venture Capital',array['$100K - $500K','$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M']::text[],array['Digital Health','Consumer']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Pre-seed']::text[],true,null,null,array['US/Canada']::text[],'https://twitter.com/IAmCharlesDKing','https://www.linkedin.com/in/charles-d-king-65179a54/','Charles D. King is founder and CEO of MACRO. Launched in 2015, MACRO is a newly formed venture that sits at the intersection of content, technology and brand curation. With a focus on creating film, television and digital content for African-American, Latino and Multicultural consumers (ALM), the company is perfectly positioned to capitalize on the explosive growth in this important market.','Los Angeles, California','2023-04-20T01:27:22.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Charles Hudson','Managing Partner','Precursor Ventures',array['$100K - $500K']::text[],array['AI','API','AR/VR','Automation','Climate','Cloud','Consumer','Creator Economy','Developer Tools','B2C/E-Commerce','Education','Enterprise','Entertainment','Future of Work','Government Technology','Hardware','Health and Wellness','Industrial','IoT','Productivity','Proptech','Robotics','B2B SaaS','Social Media','Supply Chain','Transportation','Travel','Advertising','Media/Content','Payments','Sales & CRM','Social Commerce','Social Networks','Marketplaces','Generalist','FinTech','Gaming/eSports','Direct-to-Consumer (DTC)']::text[],array['Seed','Pre-seed','Series A']::text[],true,'Bobbie Baby; Carrot Fertility; Juniper Square; Modern Health; The Athletic; Clearco; Finix; mmhmm; Superhuman; Sounding Board; Encantos; TruckMap; The Juggernaut; Goodr; Halfdays; SVAcademy','charles@precursorvc.com',array['Africa','Middle East','North Africa','Latin America','US/Canada']::text[],'https://twitter.com/chudson','https://www.linkedin.com/in/chudson/','Charles Hudson is the Managing Partner and Founder of Precursor Ventures, an early­ stage venture capital firm focused on investing in the first institutional round of investment for the most promising software and hardware companies. Prior to founding Precursor Ventures, Charles was a Partner at Uncork Capital (formerly known as SoftTech VC). He has invested in a number of noteworthy companies, including Shippo, TopHat, Vungle, Drone Deploy, The Athletic, Modern Health, Juniper Square, Noyo, Incredible Health and others.','Mountain View, California','2023-04-29T10:25:19.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Charles Moldow','General Partner','Foundation Capital',array['$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M','$500K - $1M']::text[],array['Enterprise','FinTech','Marketplaces','SaaS','SMB Software','Consumer','AI','Developer Tools','Web3','B2C/E-Commerce']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Series B+']::text[],true,'DeepFraud AI; States Title; Grabr; Mirror Emoji Keyboard; CoverWallet; Auxmoney; BTCjam; LendingHome; Rover; Rappi; Clubhouse; Lending Club','cmoldow@foundationcapital.com',array['US/Canada']::text[],'https://www.twitter.com/cmoldow?lang=en','https://www.linkedin.com/in/charlesmoldow/','Charles’ primary focus is on identifying technology trends and new user experiences that will change the financial services landscape. His thesis investing has him focused on fintech, insurtech and proptech opportunities with a crypto overlay to everything he evaluates. Charles’ public portfolio includes early-stage investments that have led to notable IPOs with DOMA (IPO 2021), Rover (IPO 2021), LendingClub (IPO 2014), OnDeck (IPO 2014) and Everyday Health (2014). In 2016, CB Insights listed Charles among The Top 100 Venture Capitalists, and Forbes named Charles to the Midas List for the second time. Charles Moldow continues to build companies that change markets. He’s always on the lookout for startups working on the next generation of fintech, marketplaces, SaaS, and consumer tech solutions and services.','Menlo Park, California','2023-05-05T16:44:08.000Z'::timestamptz),
