('Dan Abelon','Partner','Two
  Sigma Ventures',array['$100K - $500K','$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M']::text[],array['AI','Enterprise Applications','Enterprise','Health IT','IoT','Consumer','Developer Tools','Digital Health','Cybersecurity','FinTech','BioTech','Logistics','Future of Work','Web3']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Series B+']::text[],true,null,null,array['US/Canada','Latin America','Europe']::text[],'https://twitter.com/dabelon','https://www.linkedin.com/in/danabelon/','Dan joined Two Sigma Ventures in 2015 and focuses his time investing in data-driven enterprise and consumer startups. Before joining Two Sigma, Dan was an entrepreneur as well as an investor in areas such as data science, healthcare IT, and IoT. Previously, Dan co-founded SpeedDate (acquired by IAC), a live-video online dating service that used real-time matching algorithms to connect its 23 million members. Dan is very familiar with the roller coaster ride that most founders experience during their startup journeys. Earlier in his career, worked at IBM, Lazard’s Technology M&A Group, and briefly at the World Bank in the Philippines researching investments in both technology and bamboo processing. Dan started his career as founder of the Campus Pages, a phone directory publishing business.','Brooklyn, New York','2023-04-21T00:32:32.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Dan Ahrens','Managing Partner','Left Lane Capital','{}',array['B2C/E-Commerce','Digital Health','FinTech','Marketplaces','EdTech','Proptech','Future of Work']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Series B+']::text[],true,null,null,array['US/Canada','Europe','Latin America','Africa','India','Australia/New Zealand','Asia-Pacific','Israel','Middle East','North Africa']::text[],null,'https://www.linkedin.com/in/dan-ahrens-bb77a337/','Dan joined Insight in 2016. He previously worked as a strategy consultant at the Boston Consulting Group in Philadelphia, where he advised clients in the financial services, retail, and consumer goods industries. His projects covered a variety of functional topics, including long-term growth strategy, sales force effectiveness, and operating modeldesign. Dan graduated from Duke University with degrees in Economics and Political Science, and a minor in Mathematics. Born and raised in St. Louis, MO, Dan spends his free time watching and playing basketball and soccer, cooking, and traveling.','New York, New York','2023-04-21T00:33:31.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Dan Kimerling','Managing Partner','Deciens Capital',array['$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M']::text[],array['InsureTech','Proptech','FinTech']::text[],array['Seed','Pre-seed']::text[],false,'Chipper Cash; Treasury Prime; True Link','dan@deciens.com',array['Global']::text[],'https://twitter.com/dkimerling','https://www.linkedin.com/in/dkimerling/','Dan Kimerling started Deciens because of the realization that there was (and, other than Deciens, is) no venture capital fund focused on supporting fintech companies at the seed stage. Having helped start three companies and invested in over forty, he thought that this was a major problem for founders trying to re-shape a sector that is over 20% of global GDP. Until September 2017, Dan was a senior executive at Silicon Valley Bank responsible for API Banking, Open Platform, and Global Research and Development. He joined Silicon Valley Bank in July of 2015 through the acquisition of Standard Treasury, which he co-founded and served as the CEO. Standard Treasury - a YCombinator company - was the leading provider of API solutions to the financial services community','Chicago, Illinois','2023-04-20T23:03:06.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Dan Marlo','Managing Partner','4DX Ventures',array['$0 - $100K','$100K - $500K']::text[],array['Enterprise']::text[],array['Pre-seed','Seed','Series A']::text[],true,null,null,array['US/Canada','Africa']::text[],'https://twitter.com/daniel_marlo','https://www.linkedin.com/in/daniel-marlo-b4b2b6','Dan works with 4DX portfolio companies to grow revenue, build effective teams, develop unique products and establish strategic relationships with financial, technology and business development partners, in order to rapidly scale businesses. He is passionate about working with talented management teams at companies that are at growth inflection points. Previously, Dan founded and built large global businesses across financial, technology and telecom sectors predominantly focused on emerging markets, including as Founder and CEO of Unidos, a leading provider of global financial services products that processed billions of dollars of payments. Dan currently serves as a Senior Advisor to Silver Lake, a global technology investment firm. He has also served as an active investor, advisor, director and consultant to a number of companies in fintech, sports, logistics, ecommerce, healthtech, data, edtech, gaming, marketplace and payments with multiple successful exits.','New York, New York','2023-04-21T00:39:11.000Z'::timestamptz),
