('David Cowan','Partner','Bessemer Venture Partners',array['$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M','$10M - $50M']::text[],array['Cloud Infrastructure','Enterprise','Security','Space','SMB Software','Consumer','AI','Developer Tools','Cybersecurity','BioTech','Digital Health','FinTech']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Series B+']::text[],true,'Iris Automation; Contractbook; Inc.; Auth0; DroneDeploy; Impossible Aerospace; Smule; Reputation.com; Claroty','david@bvp.com',array['US/Canada','Israel','Asia-Pacific','Europe']::text[],'https://twitter.com/davidcowan','https://www.linkedin.com/in/davidjcowan/','David Cowan is one of the world’s leading investors, having funded Seed, Series A, and Series B rounds that led to over 30 IPOs. David was ranked sixth on the Midas List and tied for fourth in the Midas List of Hall of Fame. David has co-founded three cybersecurity companies incubated within Bessemer’s offices: VeriSign (NASDAQ: VRSN), serving as initial Chairman and CFO; Good Technology (fka Visto, acquired by Blackberry) serving as CEO; and Defense.net (acquired by F5). He earned an AB in computer science / mathematics and an MBA, both from Harvard University. Today he serves on several non-profit boards including the Center for Inquiry and the Smithsonian Center for Astrophysics. He is the co-writer of the Silicon Valley mockumentary series “Bubbleproof,” and producer of the award-winning MTV Documentary film “Afghan Dreamers.”','Redwood City, California','2023-04-20T23:03:06.000Z'::timestamptz),
('David Dorsey','Partner','11.2 Capital',array['$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M']::text[],array['AI','Analytics','Cloud Infrastructure','Developer Tools','Robotics','Security','BioTech','DeepTech','Digital Health','Climate']::text[],array['Pre-seed','Seed','Series A','Series B+']::text[],true,null,null,array['US/Canada']::text[],'https://twitter.com/David__Dorsey','https://www.linkedin.com/in/davidjdorsey','David is excited about helping early-stage founders commercialize innovative technology and research. He loves to dive into technical details, and to help find use cases and product-market fit. Before joining 11.2 Capital, David was a Principal at Osage University Partners (OUP), where he invested in university spinouts and developed relationships with founders working on cutting edge research in machine learning, data, and advanced computing. Before OUP, he was a lead engineer at Lockheed Martin''s Advanced Technology Labs (ATL) where he served as principal investigator for DARPA programs applying ML to RF spectrum applications. While at Lockheed, he collaborated with university labs and industry partners to design, develop, and pursue transition opportunities for early concept technologies.','Philadelphia, Pennsylvania','2023-04-27T18:54:25.000Z'::timestamptz),
('David Evans','General Partner','Sentiero Ventures',array['$100K - $500K']::text[],array['AI','Analytics','Automation','Developer Tools','B2C/E-Commerce','Enterprise','Industrial','Proptech','B2B SaaS','Cloud Infrastructure','Data Services','Enterprise Applications','Health IT','Real Estate','SaaS','FinTech']::text[],array['Seed','Pre-seed']::text[],false,'Accel Robotics; Data Sentinel; Workplace Arcade','david@sentiero.vc',array['US/Canada']::text[],'https://twitter.com/compulsivestart','https://www.linkedin.com/in/davidevansct/','David Evans is the Managing Partner of Sentiero Ventures, an early-stage venture fund that invests in artificial intelligence enabled software businesses. He is a serial entrepreneur & technologist who started coding at 14, launched his first company at 19, and has exited multiple times as a founder and investor, including a national digital signage network that was sold to CBS and an Inc 500 eCommerce company that was sold to a strategic buyer. In addition, David is the facilitator of the CometX Accelerator for student entrepreneurs at the University of Texas at Dallas and works as an advisor to multiple startups and accelerators. David is a graduate of the University of Connecticut, a former Beneficial Hodson Scholar at Johns Hopkins University, holds a Certificate in Corporate Finance from Harvard University.','Dallas, Texas','2023-04-20T23:03:06.000Z'::timestamptz),
