('David Hirsch','Managing Partner','Compound; Compound
  Ventures',array['$100K - $500K','$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M']::text[],array['BioTech','Web3','DeepTech','Enterprise','AI','Developer Tools']::text[],array['Seed','Series A']::text[],true,'Artemis; Social Native; Speakizi; Switch; DigitalGenius; Zodiac; Move Loot; Cord Project','david@compound.vc',array['US/Canada','Europe']::text[],'http://twitter.com/startupman','https://www.linkedin.com/in/davidhirsch2/','Prior to co-founding Compound, David spent his entire career leading sales and BD teams for tech companies working alongside engineering and product functions to commercialize the company''s products and spearheading monetization. Google brought on David as their second employee in the New York headquarters in 2000 at a time when the company doing just under $3M in revenue. David then spearheaded the company''s monetization strategy by co-founding Google''s Vertical Markets Group and wiring the regional sales team structure. For eight years, he oversaw cross-functional and cross-business responsibilities, all of which helped him to lead both Google''s culture committee and its recruiting initiative and subsequently hire many of the people who lead Google''s sales and business teams today.','New York, New York','2023-04-21T19:20:41.000Z'::timestamptz),
