('Jixun Foo','Global Managing Partner','GGV Capital',array['$3M - $10M']::text[],array['Enterprise','Social Commerce','Social Networks','B2C/E-Commerce','FinTech','Web3','Proptech','Future of Work']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Series B+']::text[],true,'Moore Threads; Black Lake Technologies; Kuaidian Yuedu; Taos Data; Qingzhu; Telio.vn; Iwjw; Vdaifu; Grab',null,array['US/Canada','Latin America','Asia-Pacific','India','Africa','Israel']::text[],null,'https://www.linkedin.com/in/jixun-foo-a25aba21/','A Singaporean scholar turned venture capitalist, Jixun leads GGV Capital’s global investment team and oversees its sector-focused investment strategy. Consistently recognized among the top VCs in Asia, completed four new IPOs in 2021 alone, and serves on the board of directors for SGInnovate, an accelerator funded by the Singaporean government to help entrepreneurial scientists. Jixun has been recognized by Forbes China as one of the “Best Venture Capitalists” every year since 2006 and was also named as one of the Top 10 Venture Capitalists by Zero2IPO as well as "VC Professional of the Year" by the Asia Venture Capital Journal. He has been named to the global Forbes Midas list since 2019, and was also recognized among the Top 100 Venture Capitalists by The New York Times/CBInsights in 2019.','China','2023-04-26T08:49:24.000Z'::timestamptz),
('JJ Aguhob','Partner','Progression Fund','{}',array['Consumer','Gaming/eSports','AR/VR','Marketplaces','Future of Work']::text[],array['Pre-seed','Seed','Series A']::text[],true,null,'jj@progression.fund',array['US/Canada','Europe','Asia-Pacific','Australia/New Zealand']::text[],'https://twitter.com/jjaguhob','https://www.linkedin.com/in/jjaguhob/','Accomplished business strategist, with more than 20+ years of experience developing innovative products and technologies for companies ranging from early stage startups to global, multi-billion dollar corporations. Inspirational team leader, with proven results in driving product evolution and growth initiatives. Talented relationship manager and negotiator, with demonstrated success in collaborating with major artists and brands. Founded, operated and scaled some of the largest, most innovative web and mobile properties in the world. Designed and launched consumer-driven, social media platforms that have garnering critical acclaim and industry accolades.','Santa Monica, California','2023-04-25T07:23:15.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Joanne Chen','General Partner','Foundation Capital',array['$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M','$500K - $1M']::text[],array['AI','AR/VR','MarketingTech','Robotics','SaaS','Developer Tools','Enterprise','FinTech','Consumer','Web3']::text[],array['Series A','Series B+','Seed']::text[],true,'Tubi; findera; Jasper AI; CaptivateIQ',null,array['US/Canada']::text[],'https://twitter.com/joannezchen','https://www.linkedin.com/in/joanne-chen-8486677','Joanne’s passion for technology developed early, when her mathematician dad and computer scientist mom taught her how to program. By the time she was nine years old, she had turned her skills into a business and made her first webpage for a client. Joanne began her career as an engineer at Cisco Systems and later co-founded a mobile gaming company. Joanne was on the boards of TubiTV (acquired by Fox for $500m) and Mya (acquired by Stepstone), and is currently on the board of and/or invested in Tonkean, Jasper.AI, SafelyYou, EraDB, CaptivateIQ, Oasis Labs, Watchful and others. Joanne studies the impact of AI on the enterprise and invests in AI-first B2B applications and data platforms that are the building blocks of the automated enterprise. She has shared her learnings as a featured speaker at conferences including CES, SXSW, WebSummit, and has spoken about the impact of AI on society in her TED talk “Confessions of an AI Investor.”','San Francisco, California','2023-04-26T08:56:53.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Jocelyn Goldfein','Managing Director','Zetta Venture Partners',array['$100K - $500K','$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M','$0 - $100K']::text[],array['AI','Analytics','Cloud Infrastructure','Diverse Investors','Enterprise']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Series B+']::text[],true,'Aptology; Promethium; Opsani; Nutanix Beam; Tallyfy; Yotascale; Townsquared; AppVirality; Domino Data Lab; Fixie.ai; Tractable; Verusen; Kaggle','jocelyn@zettavp.com',array['US/Canada']::text[],'https://twitter.com/jgoldfein','https://www.linkedin.com/in/jgoldfein/','I''m personally keenly interested in cloud infrastructure, DevOps, security, supply chain & logistics, and tech that transforms industries. I''ve spent my career building software in the formative years of companies like VMware and Facebook (as well as a few startups). I''ve spanned a broad set of domains from operating systems to consumer web and mobile apps to shrink-wrapped software to developer tools to big data. The one "constant" has been high-growth and industry transformation. I''m passionate about scaling products, teams, and companies, and I care deeply about STEM education.','Los Angeles, California','2023-04-26T11:42:46.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Joe Lonsdale','General Partner','8VC; Anduin
  Ventures',array['$100K - $500K','$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M','$10M - $50M']::text[],array['BioTech','Enterprise','FinTech','GovTech','Health IT','Logistics','SaaS','Consumer','AI','Developer Tools','Digital Health','Defense, Gov, & Legal','Financial Services','B2C/E-Commerce','Generalist']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Pre-seed','Series B+']::text[],true,'Pipe; Anduril; Flexport; Cityblock Health','joe.lonsdale@swayvc.com',array['US/Canada']::text[],'https://twitter.com/JTLonsdale','https://www.linkedin.com/in/joe-lonsdale-6695a2/','Before focusing on institutional investing, Joe co-founded Palantir (NASDAQ: PLTR) a global software company known for its work in defense and other industries, as well as for providing the platform to run the COVID-19 common operating picture for key decision makers in over 35 countries. After Palantir, he founded and remains as Chairman of both Addepar, which has over $4 trillion USD on its wealth management technology platform, and OpenGov, which provides software for over 2,000 municipalities and state agencies. More recently, he is also a co-founder of Affinity, Epirus, Resilience Bio, and other mission-driven technology companies, which he continues to create with his team out of the 8VC Build program.','Austin, Texas','2023-04-26T11:48:07.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Joe Morrissey','General Partner','Andreessen Horowitz',array['$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M','$10M - $50M']::text[],array['AI','Developer Tools','Cybersecurity','Web3','DeepTech','BioTech','Digital Health','Consumer','FinTech','Gaming/eSports','AR/VR']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Series B+']::text[],true,null,null,array['Asia-Pacific','US/Canada']::text[],'https://twitter.com/morrisseyjoe','https://www.linkedin.com/in/morrisseyjoe/','Prior to joining a16z, Joe was chief revenue officer at Segment, where he scaled revenues to upwards of $200M ARR in advance of the company’s $3.2B acquisition by Twilio. Before Segment, he was was the EMEA vice president and general manager for three open source software companies: Hortonworks, which combined with Cloudera in a $5.2B merger in 2019; MongoDB, which went public in 2017; and MySQL, which was acquired by Sun Microsystems for $1B in 2008.','San Francisco, California','2023-04-26T11:55:37.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Joe Proto','Co-Founder','Windham
  Venture Partners',array['$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M']::text[],array['Digital Health']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Series B+']::text[],true,null,null,array['US/Canada']::text[],null,'https://www.linkedin.com/in/joproto/','Joe Proto became Chairman and Chief Executive Officer of Transactis Inc. in 2007, after nearly three decades in the billing and payments industry as a senior executive and successful entrepreneur. Prior to Transactis, he launched REMITCO, a remittance processing company, which was acquired in 2000 by First Data Corp, as well as Financial Telesis (CashFlex), which was acquired in 1992 by CoreStates, now part of Wells Fargo. Joe recently joined the Board of Directors of BillMyParents and is also an LP and Advisor in Metamorphic Ventures (focused on transactional media). Joe is a member of various financial services associations and has been a frequent speaker at conferences in the payments industry.','Jacksonville, Florida','2023-04-26T11:58:49.000Z'::timestamptz),
