  Capital',array['$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M']::text[],array['AI','Analytics','API','AR/VR','Automation','Climate','Cloud','Consumer','Crypto/Blockchain','Developer Tools','B2C/E-Commerce','Education','Enterprise','Entertainment','Future of Work','Government Technology','Health and Wellness','Healthcare/Medtech','Industrial','IoT','Media','Productivity','Proptech','Robotics','B2B SaaS','Social Media','FinTech','Marketplaces','Gaming/eSports','Direct-to-Consumer (DTC)']::text[],array['Pre-seed','Seed','Series A']::text[],false,'BacklotCars; Cypress.io; Emotive; On Running; Pleo; Sift','joe@muckercapital.com',array['Global']::text[],'https://twitter.com/joetsai24','https://www.linkedin.com/in/joe-tsai/','Joe focuses on early stage investments, particularly in software, fintech and marketplaces. Previously, Joe was a Vice President on the investment team at Stripes, where he invested in companies including On Running (NYSE: ONON), BacklotCars (acquired by KAR), Cypress.io, Emotive, Pleo, and Sift. Prior to Stripes, Joe was a management consultant in McKinsey''s business technology practice, where he advised Fortune 500 clients on digital strategy and transformation topics including eCommerce enablement, online customer journeys, and data analytics and IT infrastructure. Earlier, Joe was one of the first research analysts at CB Insights, where he delved into the industry of startups and venture capital while working within what was then a ~10 person startup itself. A graduate of the University of Pennsylvania''s Jerome Fisher Program in Management and Technology, Joe holds a BS in Economics from the Wharton School and a BAS in Computer Science from Penn Engineering.','Los Angeles Metropolitan','2023-04-29T10:25:19.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Joel Cutler','Managing Director','General Catalyst',array['$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M','$10M - $50M']::text[],array['Digital Health','Consumer','Enterprise','Web3','FinTech']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Series B+']::text[],true,'Airbnb; Lemonade','jcutler@generalcatalyst.com',array['Latin America','India','US/Canada']::text[],'https://twitter.com/jcut','https://www.linkedin.com/in/joel-cutler-317743/','Spent entrepreneurial career building travel, specialty/targeted consumer-direct commerce and consumer fintech businesses before starting General Catalyst with friend David Fialkow In the early days of General Catalyst, partnered with Paul English and Steve Hafner to start KAYAK in to provide consumers with an easy and transparent way to purchase travel services online Currently works with companies including Airbnb (NASDAQ: ABNB), Atom Finance, BeautyPie, Cadre, Lemonade (NYSE: LMND), Multiverse, Oscar (NYSE: OSCR), Rockets of Awesome, Warby Parker and WellDot. Some of my previous investments include Freebird (acquired by Capital One), GroupMe (acquired by Skype), Handy (acquired by ANGI Homeservices), ITA Software (acquired by Google), Jet (acquired by Walmart), OLX (acquired by Naspers), Reveal Imaging (acquired by SAIC), and Venmo (acquired first by Braintree and then by eBay)','Cambridge, Massachusetts','2023-04-14T02:21:58.000Z'::timestamptz);

