('John Smothers','Investor; Partner','Acrew Capital; Scribble Ventures',array['$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M','$100K - $500K']::text[],array['AI','Analytics','API','Automation','Climate','Cloud','Consumer','Crypto/Blockchain','DeepTech','Developer Tools','Education','Enterprise','Entertainment','Future of Work','Health and Wellness','Healthcare/Medtech','Industrial','InsureTech','IoT','Life Sciences','Productivity','Proptech','Robotics','B2B SaaS','Social Media','B2C/E-Commerce','FinTech','Marketplaces','Gaming/eSports']::text[],array['Multi-stage','Pre-seed','Seed','Series A']::text[],true,'Finix; Hologram; Pipe; Prenda; Sorare; Brew.com; SteadyMD','john@acrewcapital.com',array['Global','US/Canada']::text[],'https://twitter.com/smothers_john','https://www.linkedin.com/in/john-smothers-97b258121/','John is an investor at Acrew. Prior to joining Acrew, John co-founded an eCommerce focused startup studio where he helped successfully bootstrap multiple brands. In addition to his work in the CPG industry, John co-founded Dimension Ventures, an early-stage angel fund. As an angel, he has invested in companies like Brew.com, Bito, Finix, Pipe, Hologram, Prenda, Rosebud.ai, Sorare, and others. John serves on the comms committee at BLCK VC and co-founded a restaurant development company. He strongly believes hospitality principles can carry over to the tech ecosystem. John attended the University of Delaware where he studied leadership and business in the Biden School of Public Policy and Horn Entrepreneurship program. A two-time entrepreneur who has also backed 30+ companies as an angel and institutional investor, John joined Scribble Ventures to return to his roots of partnering with founders at the earliest stages.','San Francisco, California','2023-04-26T19:02:35.000Z'::timestamptz),
('John Spinale','Managing Partner','Jazz Venture Partners',array['$0 - $100K','$100K - $500K','$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M']::text[],array['Enterprise','BioTech','Digital Health','AI','Developer Tools','Gaming/eSports','AR/VR']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Series B+']::text[],true,null,'jspinale@jazzvp.com',array['US/Canada']::text[],'https://twitter.com/jspinale','https://www.linkedin.com/in/johnspinale/','John is a proven leader in consumer technology and digital media with a career focused on building, scaling and running high-growth companies of all sizes, from initial seed through to late-stage operation. He possesses a deep understanding of building brands, creating innovative experiences and leveraging new and emerging platforms. Prior to JAZZ, John held senior operating roles in a wide array of technology companies in both the consumer and enterprise sectors. And in a distant past long forgotten, he earned a degree in engineering from Yale. John sits on the boards of several companies in the JAZZ portfolio, including Akili, Pymetrics and Outside.','United States','2023-04-26T19:04:02.000Z'::timestamptz),
('John Vrionis','Founder and Managing Partner','Unusual Ventures',array['$100K - $500K','$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M','$0 - $100K']::text[],array['Enterprise','Consumer','Crypto/Blockchain','FinTech']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Pre-seed','Series B+']::text[],true,'CoScreen; Mem Labs; BluBracket; Vivun; Kespry; Arctic Wolf; Alpha Vantage; CloudBees; Carta; Sourcegraph; Pinterest',null,array['US/Canada']::text[],'https://twitter.com/jvrionis','https://www.linkedin.com/in/johnvrionis/','A venture capitalist since 2006, John has been an early investor in over a dozen billion dollar plus companies, including: Affirmed Networks, AppDynamics, Arctic Wolf Networks, Carta, Harness, Liftoff.io, Mulesoft, Nicira, Nimble Storage, Sourcegraph, and DataStax. Inspired by successful entrepreneurs, John arrived in Silicon Valley in 2002 and worked in product management before completing his MBA at Stanford. John looks to work with entrepreneurs who have the hunger to learn and the drive to overcome difficult obstacles. In John’s words, “I believe that you learn by overcoming adversity. For me, whether it was sports, school, or in my personal and professional life, that’s been the truth. I gravitate to people who have an immense drive and the humility to keep learning.” Prior to founding Unusual Ventures, John was a General Partner at Lightspeed Venture Partners.','Menlo Park, California','2023-04-26T19:05:03.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Johnnie Yu','Associate','Listen Ventures',array['$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M']::text[],array['AR/VR','Consumer','Crypto/Blockchain','B2C/E-Commerce','Entertainment','Health and Wellness','IoT','Media','Social Media','FinTech','Marketplaces','Gaming/eSports']::text[],array['Pre-seed','Seed','Series A']::text[],false,null,'hello@johnnieyu.com',array['US/Canada']::text[],'https://twitter.com/johnnieryu','https://www.linkedin.com/in/johnnieryu/','Johnnie is a GenZ investor at Listen, an early-stage consumer VC fund behind brands like Dame, Calm, Public Goods, Factor, KiwiCo, Interior Define, and more. While obsessed with all things consumer, he is particularly interested in Web3 and brands that build at the intersection of art/culture and commerce. He is also the founder and a core team member at ConsumerDAO, a community of professional consumer founders, investors, and brand geeks passionate about bridging Consumer + Web3.','New York, New York','2023-04-21T05:38:30.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Johnny Hu','Principal','Menlo Ventures',array['$100K - $500K','$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M']::text[],array['BioTech','Consumer','Cybersecurity','FinTech','Digital Health','Logistics','Enterprise']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Series B+']::text[],true,null,'johnny@menlovc.com',array['US/Canada']::text[],null,'https://www.linkedin.com/in/johnnyhhu/','As a principal at Menlo Ventures, Johnny invests in biotech and life science companies with a focus on novel therapeutics and new technologies for improving medical outcomes. He has firsthand experience working at the bench on engineering new tools for the clinic. While completing his Ph.D., Johnny helped develop gene editing technologies that were licensed by companies such as Editas Medicine (NASDAQ: EDIT) and Beam Therapeutics (NASDAQ: BEAM). He is excited about partnering with founders at the beginning of the company journey to translate groundbreaking science into new medicines. Prior to Menlo, Johnny was a vice president at Longitude Capital, where he made several investments in early-stage biotech companies. He was a board observer at Lexeo Therapeutics, Endeavor Biomedicines, and Opna IO, and was on the investment team for Amunix Pharmaceuticals. Before Longitude, he was an associate at Omega Funds, where he worked on the firm’s investment in Nuvation Bio (NYSE: NUVB).','San Francisco, California','2023-04-26T19:07:23.000Z'::timestamptz),
