  Capital',array['$100K - $500K','$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M']::text[],array['Healthcare/Medtech','B2B SaaS','AR/VR','Crypto/Blockchain','Consumer','B2C/E-Commerce','Education','Food and Beverage','Health IT','SaaS','FinTech','Marketplaces']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Pre-seed']::text[],false,'Gentem Health; Lambda School','jon@muckercapital.com',array['US/Canada']::text[],'https://twitter.com/jonbroscious','https://www.linkedin.com/in/jon-broscious','Prior to joining Mucker Capital, Jon spent 3.5 years at Social Starts and Joyance Partners focusing on software investments in alternative education, consumer brands and healthcare, with a particular interest in new models of distribution across patients, insurers, and providers. Before his time with Social Starts, Jon was a Director with the Advisory Board Company (acquired by Optum) and Education Advisory Board (acquired by Vista) on its internal Strategy and Operations team focusing on revenue maximization across new sales and renewals. He guided teams on new product launches, staffing optimization, market research, customer acquisition and retention, and worked with the corporate development team on several acquisitions within the healthcare provider and higher education industries. He also spent time on revenue cycle consulting with health systems across the US.','Austin, Texas','2023-04-21T00:16:39.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Jon Callaghan','Founder and Managing Partner','True Ventures',array['$100K - $500K','$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M','$10M - $50M','$0 - $100K']::text[],array['AI','BioTech','Consumer Health','Enterprise','Hardware','IoT','Material Science','Generalist','CPG/D2C','Climate','Digital Health','Consumer']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Series B+']::text[],true,'Wefarm; Aisera; The Yes; Peloton; Rise Science; MyVR; 3D Robotics; Podhero; Fitbit','jon@trueventures.com',array['US/Canada']::text[],'https://twitter.com/jcal7','https://www.linkedin.com/in/joncallaghan/','VC since 1991 and 3x founder. His first company was Mountain Bike Outfitters, Inc., which he created at age 18. Before founding True, Jon was a managing director at Globespan Capital Partners. recently the Chairman of the National Venture Capital Association.','Palo Alto, California','2023-04-26T19:13:22.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Jon Dishotsky','Investment Partner','Giant Ventures',array['$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M']::text[],array['Climate','Health and Wellness','FinTech','Digital Health']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Pre-seed','Series B+']::text[],true,'Block; Calm.com; Mercury; Mighty Buildings; Radicle; Say','jon@giant.vc',array['Global','US/Canada','Europe']::text[],'https://twitter.com/jondishotsky?lang=en','https://www.linkedin.com/in/jondishotsky/','Jon is an early-stage investor and mentor focusing on pre-seed and seed. He was previously the co-founder and CEO of Starcity, a global coliving company that raised over $50M in venture capital and was backed by Bullpen Capital, Deciens, NEA, Social Capital, and Y Combinator. Starcity was acquired by Common in 2021 after narrowly escaping the pandemic. He was in the YC Core batch in the Summer of 2016 and the YC Growth batch in the Winter of 2019. He has two core focus areas right now: He is a Venture Partner (EIR) at Giant Ventures (Giant.vc). This multi-stage fund invests in companies solving the world’s most pressing challenges: Environment, Cities, Health & Wellbeing, and Financial Inclusion. You can learn more about the fund here: (https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2020-09-24/david-miliband-john-browne-join-purpose-driven-venture-fund). He invests out of personal capital as a generalist at the pre-seed stage. His fund, Daft Capital, focuses on mentorship, storytelling, and training of first-time founders to execute their big vision. The combined portfolio of companies includes AvantStay, Blair, Buoyant Aero, Craft Aerospace, Elix, Jupe, Marine Layer, Mercury, Mighty Buildings, Block Renovation, Remote, Ruth Health, Verifiable, and Waterplan.  previously the co-founder and CEO of Starcity, a global coliving company with locations on multiple continents, hundreds of employees, and raised over $50M in venture capital.','Sweden','2023-04-26T19:14:15.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Jon Kossow','Managing Partner','Norwest Venture Partners',array['$0 - $25K','$25K - $100K']::text[],array['IoT','SaaS','SMB Software','Consumer','Enterprise','B2C/E-Commerce','FinTech','AI','Developer Tools','EdTech','Proptech','Future of Work']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Series B+']::text[],true,'Avetta; Cority; The Rainmaker Group; Manta; 1010data; CoreLogic',null,array['US/Canada','India','Latin America']::text[],'https://www.twitter.com/GE_Jon','https://www.linkedin.com/in/jon-kossow-42706b2/','Jon joined Norwest in 2009 and brings more than 23 years of investment experience to his role as Managing Partner and Co-head of the Growth Equity team. Based in Norwest’s Palo Alto office, Jon is focused on investing across a wide range of sectors, with a particular interest in information services, software, internet, and consumer companies. His current investments include Avetta (recapitalized by Welsh, Carson, Anderson & Stowe), Clarus Commerce, CoreLogic, Cority (recapitalized by Thoma Bravo), GoFundMe, Topo Athletic, VanMoof, Vuori, Wine Access, and YipitData. Jon was previously involved with 1010data (acquired by Advance), Appriss, Classy (acquired by GoFundMe), Infutor (acquired by Verisk), Manta Media (acquired by Boostability), Rainmaker – Hospitality (acquired by Cendyn), Rainmaker – Multifamily (acquired by RealPage), The Retail Equation (acquired by Appriss), and Turnitin (acquired by Advance).','Palo Alto, California','2023-04-26T19:15:15.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Jon Sakoda','Founder','Decibel Partners',array['$100K - $500K','$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M','$10M - $50M','$50M+','$0 - $100K']::text[],array['AI','Analytics','Cloud Infrastructure','Enterprise','SaaS','Security','Social Networks','Consumer','B2C/E-Commerce']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Series B+']::text[],true,'Brandless; DataVisor; Aera Technology; HackerOne; The Players'' Tribune; ThirdLove; BlueJeans Network; Swiftype; Abacus.AI; Hearsay Systems','jon@decibel.vc',array['US/Canada']::text[],'https://twitter.com/jonsakoda','https://www.linkedin.com/in/jonsakoda/','worked alongside dozens of founders and has a passion for helping startups discover their unfair advantages. Previously a general partner at New Enterprise Associates, Jon led investments in early-stage start-ups in the consumer internet and enterprise software sectors. co-founder of IMlogic, Inc., serving as its Chief Technology Officer and Vice President of Products, through acquisition by Symantec Corporation.','Menlo Park, California','2023-04-26T19:18:44.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Jon Soberg','Managing Partner','MS&AD Ventures',array['$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M']::text[],array['AI','Analytics','Enterprise','FinTech','Impact','Insurance','IoT','Security','InsureTech','Marketplaces']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Pre-seed','Series B+']::text[],false,'Fundbox; Hippo; Next; Rubrik; Yotpo; Addepar; Braze; Jupiter; Mercury; Safe Security; InnerPlant; Pledge; Volocopter; Marble; Kountable Inc.; Hippo Insurance; Paceline; Human API',null,array['Global','US/Canada']::text[],'https://twitter.com/jon_soberg','https://www.linkedin.com/in/jonsoberg','Jon Soberg is Managing Partner at MS&AD Ventures, where he and his team invest in early stage investments in companies with great teams who are changing the world. Jon is ranked #13 on Business Insider''s Seed 100 list of top seed investors. Jon is especially interested in companies that are helping to secure a better future, including financial inclusion, risk analysis and mitigation, climate change, and security. Jon has been investing heavily in Fintech throughout his career and especially focuses on finance companies and business models that are helping people. Jon has been an early stage venture investor for over a decade and has made over 120 investments across 5 continents and has held more than 40 board positions. Many of Jon''s investments are worth billions including Addepar, Biocatch, Braze, Clubhouse, DoubleVerify (DV), Fundbox, Hippo, Next Insurance, Nutanix, REEF Technology (ParkJockey), Rubrik, STEM (STEM), Trulioo, and Yotpo. Jon Soberg prides himself on his dedication and support to the startups he funds. “I hope that I’m the trusted advisor to be the first call when one of my companies needs advice,” he said. And for Soberg, it’s more than just talk: He was an early investor in the ghost-kitchens logistics unicorn Reef and even went inside as its chief operating officer to help build out the company. Since Soberg’s initial seed investment, Reef has gone on to operate in 200 cities around the world and raised $700 million in private-equity funding in November 2020. Soberg now runs MS&AD Ventures with a focus on workplace and insurtech startups. On the side, he also works as an angel investor for startups that don’t fit the fund’s mission, such as his seed investment in Clubhouse.','Palo Alto, California','2023-04-26T19:19:34.000Z'::timestamptz),
