('Jonathan Heiliger','General Partner','Vertex Ventures',array['$100K - $500K','$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M','$10M - $50M','$0 - $100K']::text[],array['AI','Cloud Infrastructure','Data Services','Developer Tools','Enterprise','Hardware','SaaS','Security','TransportationTech']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Series B+']::text[],true,'Vintra; Very Good Security; LaunchDarkly; PerimeterX; Desktop Metal; SpaceIQ; Simppler; Hoodline; Closefactor',null,array['US/Canada','Asia-Pacific','Israel','India']::text[],'https://twitter.com/heiligerj','https://www.linkedin.com/in/jheiliger/','I was a General Partner with North Bridge Venture Partners, from April 2012 to November 2014. During my tenure I started the seed practice and led investments in Lytro, Periscope.io, Quora, and Ravel Law, in addition to co-founding Coolan. Prior to NBVP, I worked at Facebook, where I led global infrastructure, site architecture, and internal systems as VP Infrastructure & Technical Operations, from 2007 until 2012. During that time Facebook grew from 35 million to over 800 million users. Earlier in my career, I co-founded and was CTO of GlobalCenter, and later founded Global Crossing’s venture capital group. While scaling GlobalCenter, we saw an opportunity to build the world’s first native-optical IP network. I currently serve on the board of directors of Webmonsters, in addition to Vertex portfolio companies PerimeterX, CloudAcademy, and SpaceIQ.','Palo Alto, California','2023-04-26T19:28:55.000Z'::timestamptz),
