('Lainy Painter','Partner','Craft Ventures',array['$25K - $100K','$100K - $500K','$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M','$10M - $50M','$3M - $10M']::text[],array['Enterprise','Health IT','IoT','SaaS','Consumer','Marketplaces']::text[],array['Seed','Series B+','Pre-seed','Series A']::text[],true,'BounceX; Prodigy; ClickUp',null,array['US/Canada']::text[],'https://twitter.com/lainypainter','https://www.linkedin.com/in/elena-painter/','Lainy invests primarily in SaaS and Marketplaces. Prior to Craft, Lainy worked at Battery Ventures in San Francisco. Previously, Lainy worked at Gainsight, a B2B customer success startup where she helped lead business operations and strategy across the organization, including initiatives to grow services revenue and drive product adoption. Lainy started her career at Goldman Sachs on the technology, media and telecom investment banking team, advising companies including PayPal, LinkedIn, Zendesk, and 2U. Lainy is an active member of All Raise, the non-profit dedicated to increasing representation in venture capital. She served as Co-Chair for the 2018, 2019, and 2020 Women Who Venture Summits.','New York, New York','2023-04-29T15:05:17.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Lan Xuezhao','Founder and Managing Partner','Basis Set Ventures',array['$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M']::text[],array['AI','API','AR/VR','Automation','Climate','Cloud','Creator Economy','Crypto/Blockchain','DeepTech','Developer Tools','B2C/E-Commerce','Education','Enterprise','Entertainment','Food and Beverage','Future of Work','Government Technology','Hardware','Health and Wellness','Healthcare/Medtech','Industrial','IoT','Productivity','Proptech','Robotics','B2B SaaS','Social Media','Supply Chain','Transportation','Travel','FinTech','Marketplaces','Gaming/eSports']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Pre-seed']::text[],true,'Path; Rasa; Scale; Workstream; Verge Genomics; Rutter',null,array['Global','US/Canada','Asia-Pacific']::text[],'https://twitter.com/xuezhao','https://www.linkedin.com/in/lan-xuezhao-50aa1a1/','Founder of Basis Set, the largest seed fund raised by a solo GP in 2017. Lan built and led the Corporate Development Strategy team at Dropbox during its most acquisitive time. She previously managed teams at McKinsey in New York and Shanghai, advising Fortune 500 companies on issues including big data, AI, and growth strategy. Earlier in her career, Lan designed and developed brain training games as a founder and studied human brain functions for her Ph.D. She also received her M.A. in Statistics, both from the University of Michigan.','San Francisco, California','2023-04-21T05:38:30.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Larry Bohn','Managing Director','General Catalyst',array['$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M','$10M - $50M']::text[],array['Digital Health','Consumer','Enterprise','Web3','FinTech']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Series B+']::text[],true,'Hubspot','lbohn@generalcatalyst.com',array['Latin America','India','US/Canada']::text[],'https://twitter.com/larrybohn','https://www.linkedin.com/in/labohn/','Investment focus today includes new and existing businesses in cloud-based computing, AI, and SaaS business models, especially with a focus on commerce and analytic applications Built three leading business software companies before joining General Catalyst, taking two of them through their IPOs as CEO','Arlington, Massachusetts','2023-04-20T23:03:06.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Lars Albright','General Partner','Unusual Ventures',array['$100K - $500K','$0 - $100K']::text[],array['Enterprise','Consumer','FinTech']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Pre-seed','Series B+']::text[],true,'Skydio',null,array['US/Canada']::text[],'https://twitter.com/larsalbright','https://www.linkedin.com/in/larsalbright/','Lars is a General Partner at Unusual Ventures and leads investments in consumer software, fintech and vertical SaaS. He loves to work with founders who have the unique blend of passion and persistence, coupled with humility and a desire to learn. Lars is a repeat entrepreneur and has spent his career building successful high growth companies as a founder, executive and investor. The last two venture-backed businesses Lars co-founded were acquired by Apple and Mastercard, respectively. Lars looks for entrepreneurs that confront challenges head on, take action and embrace the accountability that comes with starting a business and managing a team.','Boston, Massachusetts','2023-04-29T15:17:20.000Z'::timestamptz),
