('Lee Ainslie','Founder','Maverick Ventures','{}',array['Digital Health','Consumer']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Series B+']::text[],true,null,null,array['US/Canada']::text[],null,null,'Mr. Lee S. Ainslie III is a Managing Partner at Maverick Capital Ltd. He founded the firm in 1993. Prior to this, Mr. Ainslie was a Managing Director at Tiger Management Corporation. He was employed at KPMG Peat Marwick as a Consultant for that firm''s National Director of Information Technology. Mr. Ainslie is a Vice Chairman and Director ofthe Robin Hood Foundation. He is a Trustee of the Episcopal High School and a Member of the Advisory Board of the University of Virginia''s Alumni Association. Mr. Ainslie earned an M.B.A. from the University of North Carolina, beta gamma sigma. He earned a B.S. in Systems Engineering from the University of Virginia, a Westmoreland Davis Scholar and is a Thomas Pinckney Bryan Jr. scholar','Alexandria, Virginia','2023-04-29T15:51:54.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Lee Carter','Partner','Equal Opportunity (EO) Ventures',array['$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M']::text[],array['AgTech','CleanTech/Environment','Cloud Infrastructure','Data Services','EnergyTech','Enterprise','Hardware','Insurance','IoT','Logistics','Manufacturing','FinTech','Digital Health','AI','Developer Tools','EdTech','Climate','Proptech','Defense, Gov, & Legal','Under-represented founders']::text[],array['Series A','Pre-seed','Seed']::text[],true,'Kolmostar; BRCK','leecarter@eoventures.com',array['US/Canada']::text[],'https://twitter.com/leecarter90','https://www.linkedin.com/in/leecarter90/','Seasoned finance professional, with extensive experience building businesses, investing in early-stage tech startups, and helping them grow. Experience across product Venture Capital, corporate development, finance, hr, operations, and investor relations','Seattle, Washington','2023-04-29T15:53:55.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Lee Edwards','Partner','Root Ventures',array['$1M - $3M']::text[],array['AI','Developer Tools','DeepTech']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Series B+']::text[],true,null,null,array['US/Canada','Africa']::text[],'https://twitter.com/terronk','http://www.linkedin.com/in/leeredwards','I invest in engineers who are starting companies that tackle the hard problems in software developer tools and services, software infrastructure, applied AI & ML, tooling for data scientists and engineers, computer vision, and anything else that takes a strong technical team to build. We invest $1-2M checks at the Seed/Pre-Seed/Post-Seed stage any time we can be a lead/co-lead sized investor in a $1-4M round.','San Francisco, California','2023-04-14T08:55:42.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Lee Hower','Co-Founder and Partner','NextView Ventures',array['$100K - $500K','$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M']::text[],array['Consumer','Digital Health','Proptech','FinTech','Enterprise']::text[],array['Pre-seed','Seed']::text[],true,null,'lee@nextviewventures.com',array['US/Canada']::text[],'https://twitter.com/leehower','https://www.linkedin.com/in/leehower/','He has spent his entire career as an entrepreneur and investor in early-stage software and internet startups. Lee started his career as an early employee of PayPal in product and business development roles, through the company’s 2002 IPO and sale to eBay. After PayPal, Lee was a co-founder of LinkedIn (NYSE: LNKD) and served as head of corporate development during the company’s early years.','Boston, Massachusetts','2023-04-29T15:55:16.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Lee Jacobs','Founder and General Partner','Long Journey Ventures',array['$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M','$0 - $100K','$100K - $500K']::text[],array['Angel','Scout','and Solo-Capitalists','Consumer']::text[],array['Seed','Pre-seed','Series A']::text[],true,'Anduril; Checkr; COMP (Compound); Loom; Rappi; Crusoe Energy; Mindbloom; PopShop Live; Wonderschool; Common Networks; Pipefy; Deno',null,array['Global','US/Canada']::text[],'https://www.twitter.com/leejacobs','https://www.linkedin.com/in/lee-jacobs/','Lee''s personal mission is to help people become the best versions of themselves. Specializes in providing support with fundraising, coaching, and connecting entrepreneurs to world class operators so they can build for the long term.','San Francisco, California','2023-04-14T08:57:11.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Lee Linden','Managing Partner','Quiet Capital',array['$100K - $500K','$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M']::text[],array['Angel','Scout','and Solo-Capitalists','Enterprise','AI','Developer Tools','Web3','FinTech']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Pre-seed']::text[],true,'Holloway; NUGGS; Golden; Outlaw; Agora; Peptalk; Elucd; ScopeAI; Rippling; MasterClass; Color; Sift; Flexport; Gusto; Cruise; PlanGrid; Point',null,array['US/Canada']::text[],'http://twitter.com/lclinden','https://www.linkedin.com/in/lclinden/','Previously lead Facebook''s emerging initiatives in commerce, including Gifts and the Facebook Card. Lee also founded Karma, a breakthrough mobile commerce platform which allowed smartphone users to instantly send real gifts to others without the burden of physical mailing addresses. Karmawas acquired by Facebook in early 2012. Prior to Karma, Lee founded Tapjoy and piloted the company to its position as a leading mobile advertising platform which today touches more than 1 billion devices. He began Tapjoy by co-creating multiple top mobile games for iOS/Android and subsequently unraveling the potential of mobile advertising and app distribution at scale. Earlier, Lee worked for venture capital firm Kleiner Perkins and helped launch the iFund, a $100M investment vehicle focused on smartphone application platforms.','New York, New York','2023-04-29T15:56:28.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Lee Shapiro','Managing Partner','7wire Ventures',array['$100K - $500K','$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M','$0 - $100K']::text[],array['Digital Health']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Series B+']::text[],true,null,'lee@7wireventures.com',array['US/Canada']::text[],null,'https://www.linkedin.com/in/leeshapiro/','He served as Chief Financial Officer of Livongo Health [NASDAQ:LVGO] until November 2020. Previously he was President of Allscripts [NASDAQ:MDRX] from 2001 until the end of 2012. His leadership was integral in the execution of over $4B in mergers, acquisitions, and financings. His responsibilities included the company’s strategy, international operations, business development and partnerships, legal, government relations, and health plan initiatives. Prior to stepping in as CFO of Livongo and leading its 2019 IPO, Lee served on the board of the company since its launch, chaired the audit committee, and served as a member of its compensation committee.','Sarasota, Florida','2023-04-29T17:43:49.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Leif Danielsen','Partner','Acequia Capital (AceCap)',array['$100K - $500K','$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M','$0 - $100K']::text[],array['Generalist','BioTech','FinTech','B2C/E-Commerce','Logistics','Enterprise','EdTech','AI','Developer Tools']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Pre-seed']::text[],true,null,null,array['US/Canada','Europe']::text[],'https://twitter.com/LeifDanielsen','https://www.linkedin.com/in/leif-danielsen-35a56550/','Leif focuses on early stage investment strategy and company building. He lives in Seattle, WA and prior to COVID he could be found either in the mountains or huddling at the closest wifi router in Berlin Tegel Airport.','Seattle, Washington','2023-04-29T17:45:03.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Leigh Marie Braswell','Principal','Founders Fund',array['$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M','$10M - $50M']::text[],array['AI','Developer Tools','DeepTech','BioTech','Enterprise','Climate','Consumer','Hardware']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Series B+']::text[],true,null,null,array['US/Canada']::text[],'https://twitter.com/lm_braswell','https://www.linkedin.com/in/leigh-marie-braswell','Leigh was an early engineer & the first product manager at Scale AI, where she originally built & later led product development for the LiDAR/3D annotation products, used by many autonomous vehicles, robots, and AR/VR companies as a core step in their machine learning lifecycles. She also has done software development at Blend, machine learning at Google, and quantitative trading at Jane Street. Leigh Marie is originally from Alabama, graduated from MIT, and loves to play poker, run long distances, and scuba dive.','San Francisco, California','2023-04-18T20:07:43.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Lenny Pruss','General Partner','Amplify Partners',array['$100K - $500K','$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M']::text[],array['AI','Cloud Infrastructure','Developer Tools','Enterprise','Security','Cybersecurity']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Series B+']::text[],true,'Strangeworks; Cockroach Labs; Anyscale; dbt Labs; Elementl; Sourcegraph; Chainguard; Temporal Technologies','lenny@amplifypartners.com',array['US/Canada']::text[],'https://twitter.com/lennypruss','https://www.linkedin.com/in/lennypruss/','Lenny started his VC career in New York at the height of the social and mobile booms where seemingly the entire tech world was chasing the next Instagram or WhatsApp. To him, technology was always about leverage, enabling us to do more with less, to build better, faster, and cheaper, and unlock new applications and services. Fast forward a decade later, and his exploration of cloud computing, DevOps, data infrastructure, and security led me to work with generational founders of companies like Datadog, Hashicorp, and Cockroach Labs.','San Francisco, California','2023-04-29T17:47:30.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Leo Banchik','Partner','Global Founders Capital',array['$500K - $1M']::text[],'{}',array['Seed','Pre-seed']::text[],true,'Found Energy',null,array['US/Canada','Latin America','India','Asia-Pacific','Europe','Africa','Israel','Australia/New Zealand','Middle East','North Africa']::text[],null,'https://www.linkedin.com/in/leobanchik/','Leo Banchik is a partner @ Global Founders Capital focused on climate tech. Before GFC, he lead climate tech investing work @ McKinsey Sustainability and earned a PhD in Mechanical Engineering','San Francisco, California','2023-04-29T17:52:23.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Leo De Luna','Angel Investor',null,array['$100K - $500K','$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M']::text[],array['Enterprise','SaaS','Consumer','Commercial Services']::text[],array['Seed','Pre-seed','Series B+']::text[],true,'SpyCloud; Iris Automation; BlackDuck',null,'{}','https://www.twitter.com/leoofthemoon?lang=en','https://www.linkedin.com/in/leo-de-luna-313226/',null,'New York, New York','2023-04-14T22:45:06.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Leo Polovets','Co-Founder and General Partner','Susa Ventures',array['$1M - $3M','$500K - $1M']::text[],array['Healthcare/Medtech','B2B SaaS','AI','Data Services','Education','Enterprise','Health & Hospital Services','Insurance','Logistics','SaaS','Marketplaces','FinTech','Digital Health','Consumer','DeepTech']::text[],array['Seed','Pre-seed','Series A','Series B+']::text[],true,'Flexport; Outlier; Pex; Robinhood; Scalyr; Stedi; Gentem; Spiketrap; Unioncrate; Holloway; FuzzBuzz; Smile Identity; ScopeAR','leo@susaventures.com',array['US/Canada','Africa','Latin America','India']::text[],'https://twitter.com/lpolovets','https://www.linkedin.com/in/lpolovets/','I''m a co-founder and General Partner at Susa Ventures. I invest across sectors, but mostly focus on b2b companies. A few specific sectors I''ve invested in heavily are enterprise software; developer tools and technical products; and logistics and supply chain. I led Susa''s investments in dozens of companies, including Outlier, Pex, Scalyr, and Stedi. Having been a software engineer for 10+ years, I approach challenges with an engineering mindset and support portfolio companies in vetting and hiring technical talent. Prior to Susa, I was the second engineering hire at Linkedin where I helped build the first versions of products like LinkedIn Jobs and LinkedIn Groups. I then worked on payment fraud detection algorithms at Google, and was also an early engineer at Factual, where I built data cleaning, processing, and deduping software. Focuses on enterprise software; developer tools and technical products; and logistics and supply chain. Led Susa''s investments in Outlier, Pex, Scalyr, and Stedi. Prior to Susa, Leo was the second engineering hire at Linkedin where he worked on the first versions of products like LinkedIn Jobs and LinkedIn Groups. Leo then worked on payment fraud detection algorithms at Google, and was also an early engineer at Factual, where he built data processing software. Leo received a bachelor''s degree in Engineering and Applied Science (Computer Science) from Caltech.','Miami, Florida','2023-04-29T17:55:36.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Les Craig','General Partner','Next
  Frontier Capital',array['$10M - $50M','$50M+']::text[],array['Developer Tools','Enterprise','SMB Software','Consumer','DeepTech']::text[],array['Seed','Series A']::text[],true,null,null,array['US/Canada']::text[],'https://twitter.com/montanavc?lang=en','https://www.linkedin.com/in/les-craig/','Les joined Next Frontier Capital in 2017. Prior to joining NFC, Les served as the Executive Director of the Montana State University Innovation Campus.

Les moved to Montana as the result of MSU’s national search to hire a Director for the Blackstone LaunchPad, a campus based entrepreneurship program funded by the Blackstone Charitable Foundation. In the Summer of 2016, Les received funding from the Small Business Administration to launch 406 Labs, Montana’s first accelerator program.

In 2014, Les Co-founded The Twenty, a data science services company based in Bethesda, MD which operates a high-profile network of senior mathematicians and computer scientists focused on specialized project based work for clients.

Prior to The Twenty, Les Co-founded RedOwl Analytics, a software product company that built a platform for identifying trends and anomalies in the digital trail of corporations in order to combat insider threat and mitigate risk. RedOwl was acquired by Forcepoint (Raytheon) in August of 2017.

Previously, Les served as a Technical Operations Officer at the Central Intelligence Agency where he received specialized training in telecommunications and computer network operations.

Prior to his time at the CIA, Les was a member of the professional staff of the National Security Technology Department at the Johns Hopkins University Applied Physics Lab.

While on active duty, Les served on multiple special operations task forces, as well as an Aide-de-camp to a senior intelligence professional on General Stanley McChrystal’s staff at the Joint Special Operations Command.','Bozeman, Montana','2023-04-29T18:02:12.000Z'::timestamptz),
