('Marc Andreessen','Co-Founder and General Partner','Andreessen Horowitz',array['$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M','$10M - $50M','$50M+']::text[],array['AI','BioTech','Education','Enterprise','Health & Hospital Services','Health IT','IoT','SaaS','Consumer','Developer Tools','Cybersecurity','Web3','DeepTech','Digital Health','FinTech','Gaming/eSports','AR/VR']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Series B+']::text[],true,'Earli; Roblox; Pave; Dialpad; Golden; Samsara; Figma; Reddit; Asana; Twitter; Slack; Applied Intuition; Carta; Coinbase; Wealthfront',null,array['Asia-Pacific','US/Canada']::text[],'https://twitter.com/pmarca','https://www.linkedin.com/in/marc-andreessen-41686425/','Marc is an innovator and creator, one of the few to pioneer a software category used by more than a billion people and one of the few to establish multiple billion-dollar companies. He co-created the highly influential Mosaic internet browser and co-founded Netscape, which later sold to AOL for $4.2 billion. He also co-founded Loudcloud, which as Opsware, sold to Hewlett-Packard for $1.6 billion. He later served on the board of Hewlett-Packard from 2008 to 2018. Marc holds a BS in Computer Science from the University of Illinois at Urbana-Champaign.','Menlo Park, California','2023-04-30T13:26:05.000Z'::timestamptz),
