('Masha Khusid','Partner','Drive Capital',array['$3M - $10M']::text[],array['Future of Work','AI','Developer Tools','EdTech','Digital Health','Cybersecurity','FinTech']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Series B+']::text[],true,null,'masha@drivecapital.com',array['US/Canada']::text[],'https://twitter.com/masha_khusid?lang=en','https://www.linkedin.com/in/masha-khusid-45a02853','I worked hard for my Accounting degree but was reminded to dream big in my Art History courses. I moved to the west coast for my first job in investment banking, but then took a 6-month sabbatical to explore South America. After catching the startup bug at a venture-backed fintech company, I found my way back to the midwest and joined a Chicago-based venture firm. I was delighted to find that early stage investing is the perfect environment for taking thoughtful risks!','Columbus, Ohio','2023-05-01T19:21:04.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Matias Mosse','Founder and Managing Director','Starlight Ventures',array['$100K - $500K','$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M']::text[],array['CleanTech/Environment','Digital Health','EnergyTech','Health & Hospital Services','Health IT','Pharmaceuticals','Climate']::text[],array['Seed','Pre-seed']::text[],true,null,null,array['US/Canada','Europe']::text[],null,'https://www.linkedin.com/in/matiasmosse/','Founder and CEO, Star Capital; Founder and Managing Director, Starlight Ventures. Star Capital is thesis-driven private investment office. In addition to public markets, the firm deploys capital into companies involved in natural resources, real estate projects in several geographies and through Starlight Ventures, into emerging technology projects. Starlight Ventures is a venture capital firm designed to address humanity''s greatest challenges and opportunities. The firm invests early in the brightest entrepreneurs using science and technology breakthroughs to achieve progress at scale. Previously, as an entrepreneur, pioneered in the mid 90''s the creation of several of the first Internet companies in Latin America. Matías holds a BA in Economics from the University of Buenos Aires.','Miami, Florida','2023-05-01T19:23:59.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Matias Van Thienen','General Partner','Founders Fund',array['$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M','$10M - $50M','$50M+']::text[],array['AI','Developer Tools','DeepTech','BioTech','Enterprise','Climate','Consumer','Hardware']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Series B+']::text[],true,'CrowdStrike',null,array['US/Canada']::text[],null,'https://www.linkedin.com/in/mvanthienen','Matias Van Thienen is a Partner at Founders Fund. Since joining the team in 2018, he has led or played a role in the firm’s investments in Trade Republic, Modern Health, LeafLink, Figma, RigUp, Scale AI, Newfront Insurance, Luko, Belvo and Solugen. Previously he worked at Insight and CapitalG, where he invested in companies such as UiPath,CrowdStrike, Qualtrics, Looker and ezCater. He also led Corp Dev at Wallapop, a mobile marketplace in Europe, where he was responsible for strategy, fundraising and M&A. He holds a BS in Finance and Information Systems from NYU Stern. Matias is originally from Buenos Aires, and has lived in Miami, New York, Shanghai and Barcelona. He’s an avid kite surfer and skier.','Miami, Florida','2023-05-01T19:24:58.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Matt Bigge','Partner','Crosslink Capital',array['$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M']::text[],array['AI','Cloud Infrastructure','Developer Tools','Enterprise','Health IT','IoT','Robotics','Security','Space','FinTech','Digital Health','Logistics','Cybersecurity','Consumer']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Series B+']::text[],true,'Armory; ZeroNorth; Bolster Inc.; GoExpedi; Enview; Inpher.io; Bugcrowd; ProtectWise',null,array['US/Canada']::text[],'https://twitter.com/bigge/','https://www.linkedin.com/in/bigge/','focuses on venture investments in enterprise and industrial IT infrastructure, cybersecurity, and plausible science fiction. Prior to joining Crosslink, Matt was a Venture Partner with Paladin Capital was also the CEO and Co-Founder of Strategic Social Holdings (acquired by Constellis Group). Co-Founder and President of MILCOM Technologies where he led the acquisition and commercialization of over $2B of R&D used to create over ten product companies Prior to his business career, Matt served in the U.S. Army with a distinguished record as an Infantry officer and Ranger in the 10th Mountain Division.','San Francisco, California','2023-05-01T19:25:53.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Matt Bisgyer','Vice President','Energy Impact Partners',array['$3M - $10M']::text[],array['Climate','Proptech','Cybersecurity','Logistics']::text[],array['Pre-seed','Seed','Series A','Series B+']::text[],true,null,'bisgyer@energyimpactpartners.com',array['US/Canada','Europe']::text[],'https://twitter.com/mbbisgyer','https://www.linkedin.com/in/matt-bisgyer-1bb56333/','Mr. Bisgyer joined Energy Impact Partners in January 2017 and has experience both advising and investing in early stage companies. Previously, Matt worked as an analyst in Oppenheimer’s Technology Investment Banking Group where he focused on M&A advisory, restructurings and capital raising for tech, media and telecom companies. Prior to joining Oppenheimer, Matt was an analyst at Chardan Capital Markets covering semiconductor and industrial technology companies. Matt graduated from Washington University in St. Louis with a dual degree in Finance and Political Science.','New York, New York','2023-05-01T19:27:02.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Matt Brezina','General Partner','Ford Street Ventures',array['$100K - $500K']::text[],array['AI','Analytics','API','Automation','Climate','Cloud','Consumer','Crypto/Blockchain','DeepTech','B2C/E-Commerce','Education','Enterprise','Entertainment','Future of Work','Government Technology','Health and Wellness','Healthcare/Medtech','Industrial','InsureTech','IoT','Media','Productivity','Proptech','Robotics','B2B SaaS','Social Media','BioTech','FinTech','Marketplaces']::text[],array['Pre-seed','Seed','Series A']::text[],false,'Dropbox; FunctionOfBeauty; Mercury; Ring; Solugen; Karat; Rescale; Snapdocs; Tonal',null,array['Global']::text[],'https://mercury.com/investor-db/www.twitter.com/brezina','https://www.linkedin.com/in/brezina/','Matt Brezina founded, scaled & sold two startups: Xobni YC S06 (acq Yahoo), Sincerely (acq Liberty Media). Matt has been angel investing since 2008 and has backed over 80 companies including breakouts: Dropbox, Ring, FunctionOfBeauty, Solugen, Mercury, Snapdocs, Cruise, Rescale, Tonal, Karat. Matt has invested across a diverse range of markets including Marketplaces, HealthTech, B2B SAAS, Fintech, Hardware+service, Climate Tech as well as across the US, Latam, Africa, Middle East & Europe. Matt was one of the earliest scouts, deploying money for CRV & Spark Capital. Matt is hyper-involved in hiring, fundraising, positioning and product from day zero through series A, and then shifts to a founder advisory role. His goal is to be the first person founders call for advice. Matt has helped on over 12 M&A transactions. Matt also started the Penn State Summer Founders Program and is the Founder of KidSafeSF a movement to make streets safe for travel by walking & bicycle.','San Francisco, California','2023-04-21T00:16:39.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Matt Burton','Partner','QED Investors',array['$100K - $500K','$0 - $100K','$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M']::text[],array['Advertising','Analytics','SaaS','Sales & CRM','FinTech']::text[],array['Pre-seed','Seed','Series A','Series B+']::text[],true,'Bitso',null,array['Latin America','US/Canada','Europe','Asia-Pacific']::text[],'https://twitter.com/burtomd0','https://www.linkedin.com/in/matthewdanielburton','Matt has spent his career creating technologies and businesses that have transformed industries. In digital advertising he helped build, scale and optimize the Internet’s top advertising exchanges at Google, Admeld and LiveRail, which collectively handled trillions of transactions. As employee number seven at AdMeld (which was acquired by Google for $400M in 2011), Matt played a central role in all aspects of the company, from product development to sales to operations. After Google, Burton joined LiveRail (which was acquired by Facebook for $500M in 2014) where he continued to focus on programmatic exchanges.','New York, New York','2023-04-20T23:03:06.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Matt Fates','Partner','Ascent Venture Partners',array['$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M']::text[],array['AI','Analytics','Enterprise','IoT','SaaS','Security','Crypto/Blockchain','Cybersecurity','Developer Tools','Digital Health','BioTech']::text[],array['Series A','Series B+','Pre-seed']::text[],true,'Connected2Fiber; Promoboxx; Pwnie Express; Perspecsys; HubCast; StrikeIron; Interactive Supercomputing; Terascala','mfates@ascentvp.com',array['US/Canada']::text[],null,'https://www.linkedin.com/in/mfates/','Matt’s passion for new ideas and technology started at a young age, dating back to coding with an Apple IIe.  Professionally, he was drawn to venture capital as it provides the opportunity to work closely with entrepreneurs leveraging technology to solve challenging problems.  Today, he values the opportunity to be a partner to founders, developing strong relationships, reasoning through strategic issues, and supporting them in building impactful companies. Matt has worked with early stage technology driven companies since 1996, from formation stage all the way through IPO and beyond through different roles. As a venture investor and angel, either through his firm or individually, Matt has invested in over 100 companies.','Boston, Massachusetts','2023-05-01T19:30:53.000Z'::timestamptz),
