('Matt Levin','Co-Founder and Managing Partner','Verity Venture Partners',array['$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M']::text[],array['Consumer','CPG/D2C']::text[],array['Seed','Series A']::text[],true,null,null,array['US/Canada']::text[],null,'https://www.linkedin.com/in/matt-levin-vvp/','Prior to co-founding Verity Venture Partners, Matt spent over 27 years with Bain Capital, LP. He served as a Senior Advisor in its private equity business from 2016 through September 2019. From 2001 through 2015, Matt was a Managing Director in the firm’s private equity business where he co-led the North America consumer products and retail industry vertical. He also led several professional development programs for the private equity business as well as regularly served on private equity investment and portfolio management committees. Prior to joining Bain Capital in 1992, Matt was a consultant at Bain & Company, where he consulted in the consumer products and manufacturing industries.','San Francisco, California','2023-05-01T20:11:25.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Matt Murphy','Managing Director','Menlo Ventures',array['$100K - $500K','$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M','$10M - $50M']::text[],array['Cloud Infrastructure','Enterprise','Robotics','SaaS','Social Networks','BioTech','Consumer','Cybersecurity','FinTech','Digital Health','Logistics']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Series B+']::text[],true,'Vivun; Usermind; Earli; HOVER; Benchling; FireHydrant; Harness; Digits; Carta; Canvas; Envoy; TrueWork','matt@menlovc.com',array['US/Canada']::text[],'https://twitter.com/mmurph','https://www.linkedin.com/in/matt-murphy-0415543/','Matt Murphy joined Kleiner Perkins Caufield & Byers in 1999 where he focuses on multi-stage investments across mobile and cloud infrastructure technologies. Matt is either a Director or works closely with the management teams of AppDynamics, Drawbridge, Egnyte, Insidesales.com, InstartLogic, PernixData, Puppet Labs, SessionM, Shazam, andSimplivity. Previously, Matt was a Board Observer at Google (from initial investment to IPO), launched the iFund in ’08 (a collaborative initiative with Apple to build the defining applications on the iOS platform), and led KPCB’s investments in AutoNavi (Nasdaq: AMAP, 2010) and Aerohive Networks (Nasdaq: HIVE, 2014). Matt also served as a Director at Shopkick (acquired by SK Planet 2014), Pelago (acquired by Groupon in 2011), Ocarina Networks (acquired by Dell in 2010), Dash Navigation (acquired by RIM in 2009) and Peakstream (acquired by Google in 2008).','San Francisco, California','2023-05-01T20:13:42.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Matt Turck','Partner','FirstMark
  Capital',array['$100K - $500K','$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M']::text[],array['Cloud Infrastructure','Data Services','Education','Enterprise','Health & Hospital Services','Health IT','IoT','SaaS','Consumer','Marketplaces','FinTech','B2C/E-Commerce','DeepTech']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Series B+']::text[],true,'Crossbeam; Statespace; Cockroach Labs; Text IQ; HyperScience; Dataiku; Ada Support; Upgrade; ActionIQ; Hyperscience; Synthesia',null,array['US/Canada','Europe']::text[],'https://twitter.com/mattturck','https://www.linkedin.com/in/turck/','Matt Turck is a Partner at venture capital firm FirstMark, where he focuses mostly on early-stage enterprise and B2B investing. Prior to FirstMark, Matt was a startup founder, tech executive and angel investor. Most recently, he was a Managing Director at Bloomberg Ventures, the incubation arm of Bloomberg LP, which he helped start. Previously, Matt was the co-founder of TripleHop, an enterprise search software startup that was acquired by Oracle, and then an executive at Oracle following the acquisition. Matt is passionate about building communities. Since 2011, he has been running Data Driven NYC, the largest data and AI community in the US (19,000 members). He also organizes Hardwired NYC, a community focused on deep tech (7,500 members).','New York, New York','2023-05-02T04:45:47.000Z'::timestamptz),
