('Natalie Vais','Principal','Amplify Partners',array['$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M']::text[],array['Cloud Infrastructure','Data Services','Developer Tools','Enterprise','AI','Cybersecurity']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Series B+']::text[],true,null,'natalie@amplifypartners.com',array['US/Canada']::text[],'https://twitter.com/natalievais','https://www.linkedin.com/in/natalievais/','Natalie started his career as a Sales Engineer at Oracle and eventually found her way to a small analytics startup in stealth mode at the time—Interana. Mark LaRosa hired me as his first Solutions Architect. Eventually, Natalie left Interana as Director of Product to join the Core Infrastructure team at Google. She wanted to see behind the curtain on the planetary scale systems running some of the most complex infrastructure in the world—Search and Ads. There, she helped build and scale products for internal developers at Google and later Google Cloud. Natalie is drawn to founders who have taken unconventional paths—or “career swerves" since seeing the same problem in very different contexts is one of the most valuable lessons she has learned and values in others.','San Francisco, California','2023-05-03T17:14:35.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Nate Bosshard','Founder and Managing Partner','Offline Ventures',array['$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M','$10M - $50M','$100K - $500K','$500K - $1M']::text[],array['Consumer','Health and Wellness','CleanTech/Environment','Education','Entertainment & Sports','Fashion','Food and Beverage','Future of Work','Hardware','Health & Hospital Services','Parenting/Families','SMB Software','FinTech','Web3']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Pre-seed']::text[],true,'Airtable; Hims & Hers; Livongo; Ro; Robinhood; Uber; Digit','nate@offline.vc',array['US/Canada']::text[],'https://twitter.com/natebosshard','https://www.linkedin.com/in/natebosshard/','Entrepreneur, venture investor and brand builder of iconic, category-defining, multi-billion dollar consumer businesses. I''ve been a consumer leader at every stage of a company lifecycle. As an operator I''ve lead and re-positioned heritage brands through changing market dynamics, been on the IPO rocket-ship, experienced being inside of a company acquisition and integration, and have witnessed spectacular company implosion and failure first hand. I''ve helped co-found a brand from scratch, raised hundreds of millions of venture capital, worked inside a blue-chip VC firm as a partner and LP as well as personally invested in 50+ companies. Separate of my bay-area entrepreneurial adventures I was the owner of the largest independent beverage co-packer in the country and have a stake in a dozen Midwestern community banks. Today founder / GP of Offline Ventures a $160m early stage venture fund and start-up studio. Personal passions revolve around music, art, culture and fitness.','San Francisco, California','2023-05-03T17:23:45.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Nate Cooper','Managing Partner','Barrel Ventures',array['$100K - $500K']::text[],array['Consumer','B2C/E-Commerce','Food and Beverage','Supply Chain']::text[],array['Pre-seed','Seed','Series A']::text[],false,'Clove; Haus; Olipop','Nate@barrelvc.com',array['Global']::text[],null,'https://www.linkedin.com/in/nathan-cooper-2ba9aa19/','Nate started Barrel Ventures out of a passion to help others disrupt the status quo. Surrounded by entrepreneurs at a young age, Nate became an operator himself as a founder of L3 Hospitality Group and later Wise Apple, a company that set out to change kids'' lunch. Nate is a graduate of the Goizueta School of Business at Emory University and received his MBA from the Kellogg School of Management where he was awarded a Kellogg Scholarship and named a Zell Fellow. In his free time, Nate is a passionate endurance athlete and movie quote savant. He lives in Chicago and serves on the associate boards of the US Holocaust Memorial Museum and Social Venture Partners.','Chicago','2023-02-25T04:36:07.000Z'::timestamptz),
