('Pano Anthos','Founder and Managing Director','XRC Labs',array['$100K - $500K']::text[],array['AR/VR','Fashion','Local Services','Logistics','Consumer','Crypto/Blockchain','Retail','Social Commerce','B2C/E-Commerce','Enterprise','Digital Health','CPG/D2C','Web3','Climate','AI','Developer Tools','Future of Work','FinTech']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Pre-seed']::text[],true,null,'pano@xrclabs.com',array['US/Canada','Israel','Europe','Africa','Latin America','India','Asia-Pacific','Australia/New Zealand','Middle East','North Africa']::text[],'https://twitter.com/ptanthos','https://www.linkedin.com/in/panoanthos/','Pano founded XRC Labs in 2015 and is the company’s Managing Director. Prior to this, he served in a number of leadership roles for media, retail, consumer goods and industrial companies. He also founded four digital media and software startups, including Gather Education, Hangout Industries which was the first to bring video game technology and name brands to Facebook in 2007, Pantero and Syntra / ClearCross. He began his career in supply chain and trademarked the term “global logistics systems.” He received his BA from the University of Delaware and SIA from Columbia University.','New York, New York','2023-05-05T11:09:14.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Parasvil Patel','Partner','Radical Venture',array['$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M']::text[],array['AI','Analytics','API','Automation','Climate','Cloud','DeepTech','Developer Tools','Education','Enterprise','Future of Work','Healthcare/Medtech','Industrial','Robotics','B2B SaaS','FinTech','Marketplaces']::text[],array['Seed','Series A']::text[],false,'ClimateAI; Cohere; Pixel; Waabi','parasvil@radical.vc',array['US/Canada']::text[],null,'https://www.linkedin.com/in/parasvil/','Parasvil Patel is a Partner with Radical Ventures where he works with visionary entrepreneurs using AI to transform traditional industries. Prior to joining Radical, Parasvil was with KKR where he supported diligence and portfolio value creation efforts across multiple asset classes and industries. During business school, he led go-to-market and fundraising activities for an early-stage cloud startup. He received a B.Tech. in Electrical Engineering from IIT Bombay and an MBA with High Distinction from Harvard Business School, where he graduated as a Baker Scholar.','Toronto, Ontario','2023-04-21T00:16:39.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Parul Singh','Partner','Initialized Capital',array['$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M']::text[],array['AI','Analytics','API','Cloud','Consumer','Creator Economy','Crypto/Blockchain','Developer Tools','B2C/E-Commerce','Enterprise','Health and Wellness','Healthcare/Medtech','Productivity','B2B SaaS','Marketplaces','Gaming/eSports']::text[],array['Seed','Pre-seed']::text[],false,'HealthNote; Broadlume; Embark; Flume Health; HumanFirst; Running Tide','parul@initialized.com',array['US/Canada']::text[],'https://twitter.com/parulia','https://www.linkedin.com/in/parulsingh/','Parul Singh is a product-driven founder and investor with a background in engineering, product strategy, and analytics. Parul spent the past five years on the investing team at Founder Collective, a tech-focused, early-stage seed fund where she covered Boston and NYC, evaluated over 3,000 companies, and spearheaded the firm’s investments in Embark Veterinary, Broadlume, Running Tide, HumanFirst, Flume Health, and HealthNote. Prior to investing, she spent close to a decade as an engineer and product manager at the NYTimes.com, Inc. and Fast Company, and she was the founder of a learning analytics company. At Initialized, Parul will focus her investing efforts on software companies, with a special interest in the areas of healthtech, SaaS, and analytics. Parul has an undergraduate degree from Harvard College and an MBA from MIT.','Cambridge, Massachusetts','2023-04-21T05:38:30.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Pascal Cagni','Founder & CEO','C4 Ventures',array['$100K - $500K','$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M']::text[],array['CPG/D2C','Future of Work','Hardware','B2C/E-Commerce']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Series B+']::text[],true,null,null,array['US/Canada','Europe','Israel']::text[],'https://twitter.com/pascalcagni','https://www.linkedin.com/in/pascalcagni/','In 2000, Steve Jobs appointed Pascal as General Manager and Vice President for Apple EMEIA (Europe, Middle East, India and Africa). Leading a region made of more than 120 countries, he launched groundbreaking products and services such as the iPod (2001), iTunes Store (2003), iPhone (2007), the App Store (2008) and iPad (2010). Under Pascal’s leadership, EMEIA was consistently Apple’s fastest growing region, with annual sales increasing from $1.2bn in 2001 to $40bn in 2012.','France','2023-05-05T11:13:28.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Pascal Levy-Garboua','Venture Partner','Long Journey Ventures; Pascal Levy-Garboua Syndicate',array['$100K - $500K','$500K - $1M','$0 - $100K']::text[],array['Consumer']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Pre-seed']::text[],true,null,'pascal@longjourney.vc',array['US/Canada']::text[],'https://twitter.com/2pasc','https://www.linkedin.com/in/pascallevygarboua/','Pascal loves backing founders who are passionate about the problem they are solving and have unique insights into solving it. An early investor in Checkr, Notion, Wag, PayJoy, Origin, and Womply.','Paris, Île-de-France','2023-04-14T10:56:17.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Pascal Unger','Managing Partner','Darling
  Ventures',array['$100K - $500K','$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M']::text[],'{}',array['Seed','Series A']::text[],true,null,null,array['US/Canada']::text[],'https://twitter.com/PascalUnger','https://www.linkedin.com/in/pascal-unger/','Pascal specializes in enabling founders to apply strategic thinking and best-in-class practices. A dedicated and high bandwidth partner, he developed his skill set as a management consultant in technology and finance, where he worked with industry leaders on their business strategy, Go-To-Market and M&A. Swiss born, he started his career at The Boston Consulting Group in Zurich working with Switzerland’s largest banks on their strategies, business transformations and M&A activities. In 2015, he moved to San Francisco and led BCG teams for the world’s largest tech companies focusing on integrating acquisitions, restructuring sales orgs and thinking through their go-forward strategies. In parallel, he was a Venture Partner at local VCs and an early investor in Darling Ventures. Today, he gets excited about applying the structured thinking, professionalism and tools learned to work alongside entrepreneurs in the early stages of their business.','Miami, Florida','2023-05-05T12:39:25.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Pat Connolly','Co-Founder and Managing Partner','Supermoon Capital',array['$100K - $500K','$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M']::text[],array['Digital Health']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Pre-seed']::text[],true,null,null,array['US/Canada','Africa','Latin America','Asia-Pacific','Europe','India','Israel','Australia/New Zealand','Middle East','North Africa']::text[],null,'https://www.linkedin.com/in/pat-connolly-74233a/','Before founding Supermoon Capital, Pat worked at Williams-Sonoma for 37 years in a variety of roles spanning strategy, marketing, and operations.','Menlo Park, California','2023-05-05T12:41:56.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Pat Matthews','Founder & CEO','Active Capital',array['$100K - $500K','$500K - $1M']::text[],array['AI','Enterprise','FinTech','MarketingTech','SaaS','Sales & CRM','SMB Software','Developer Tools']::text[],array['Seed','Pre-seed','Series B+']::text[],true,'Back Office.co; Living Security; Vid Grid; Keen; Tenfold; Promoter.io; Testlio; Emergent One','pat@activecapital.com',array['US/Canada']::text[],'https://twitter.com/patmatthews','https://www.linkedin.com/in/pamatthe/','Pat leads the firm, makes investment decisions, and actively supports our portfolio companies through board seats, strategy sessions, and founder coaching. Pat’s career started in 1999 when he dropped out of Virginia Tech to start a dot-com with some of his best friends and college roommates. After the dot-com bubble burst, Pat and his team persevered through years of economic downturn before creating Webmail.us, a B2B SaaS company that was recognized as one of the fastest growing private companies in America by Inc. Magazine after raising just $500k in outside capital. In 2007, Webmail was acquired by Rackspace where Pat worked as an executive on the senior leadership for six years, helping Rackspace scale to $1.5 billion in annual recurring revenue.','San Antonio, Texas','2023-05-05T12:45:21.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Pat Robinson','Managing Director - Circle Up Growth Partners','CircleUp',array['$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M']::text[],array['CPG/D2C']::text[],array['Seed','Series A']::text[],true,null,null,array['US/Canada']::text[],null,'https://www.linkedin.com/in/patrick-robinson-3583576/','Pat joined CircleUp in 2013 and has held several investing and operating roles including part of the founding CircleUp Growth Partners team. Prior to joining CircleUp, Pat was an investor at Mainsail Partners a $1B+ AUM private equity firm where he focused on growth equity investments in e-commerce and software businesses.','Los Angeles, California','2023-05-05T12:57:50.000Z'::timestamptz);

