('Pete Flint','General Partner','NFX',array['$100K - $500K','$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M']::text[],array['AI','AR/VR','FinTech','Insurance','Real Estate','SaaS','SMB Software','BioTech','Web3','DeepTech','Marketplaces','Gaming/eSports']::text[],array['Seed','Pre-seed','Series A','Series B+']::text[],true,'SESO; Edgybees; La Haus; Jupiter; Incredible Health; Letâ€™s Do This; Let''s Do This; Constru; Ribbon Health','pete@nfx.com',array['US/Canada','Israel','Latin America']::text[],'https://twitter.com/peteflint','https://www.linkedin.com/in/peteflint/','Co-founder and former CEO of Trulia, one of the internet’s most successful marketplaces. He led the company from inception to one of the largest and fastest-growing real estate brands in the U.S. with more than 50 million monthly unique users and a merger with Zillow in 2015 that valued Trulia at $3.5 billion. Prior to starting Trulia, Pete was part of the founding team of lastminute.com, a leading European online travel site that was acquired in 2005 by Travelocity/Sabre Holdings for over $1 billion. These experiences gave Pete a rarely acquired understanding of what it takes to scale a company from a great idea to a $1 billion+ exit, all from a Founder’s perspective.','San Francisco, California','2023-04-21T05:38:30.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Peter Buckland','General Partner & COO','Khosla Ventures',array['$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M','$10M - $50M']::text[],array['AgTech','AI','Education','EnergyTech','Enterprise','FinTech','Health IT','Robotics','Consumer','Semiconductors','BioTech','DeepTech','Digital Health']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Series B+']::text[],true,null,'pb@khoslaventures.com',array['USA']::text[],null,'https://www.linkedin.com/in/peter-buckland-1403693/','Peter is a Partner, Managing Director and COO at Khosla Ventures. Peter has spent the last 20+ years advising founders and entrepreneurs through the full lifecycle of their companies. Prior to joining Khosla Ventures, Peter was a Partner at WilmerHale LLP, where he led the firm’s emerging growth technology practice and was responsible for buildingtheir West Coast corporate practice. During his time there, he grew the practice by 3X, completed hundreds of financing transactions and, mostly importantly, developed deep and long term relationships with amazing entrepreneurs and their teams. Peter holds a bachelor’s degree from the University of California, Santa Barbara and a J.D., magna cum laude, from the University of San Francisco. In his spare time, Peter enjoys spending time with his wife and three daughters, skiing, sailing, mountain biking and reading.','San Francisco, California','2023-05-02T22:29:38.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Peter Chernin','Co-Founder, Chairman, and CEO','The Chernin Group (TCG)',array['$0 - $100K','$100K - $500K','$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M']::text[],array['Consumer','Marketplaces','Gaming/eSports','AR/VR','FinTech','Digital Health','CPG/D2C']::text[],array['Seed','Pre-seed','Series A']::text[],true,'Medium',null,array['USA']::text[],'https://twitter.com/PeterChernin',null,'Prior to founding The Chernin Group, Peter served as President and COO of News Corp and Chairman and CEO of the Fox Group from 1996-2009. During his tenure at Fox and News Corp, Peter oversaw Fox Filmed Entertainment as the #1 studio and greenlit the two highest grossing films of all time – Titanic and Avatar. Notable television hits during Peter’s tenure as CEO of Fox Group include 24, Modern Family, and Glee, which helped 20th Century Fox Television achieve the #1 ranking in television production. He also established Fox Network as the #1 broadcast network across nearly all demos with iconic series including The Simpsons and American Idol. Peter was responsible for launching 15+ cable networks domestically, most notably FX and Fox Sports nets. He also launched 150+ international channels and oversaw the growth of the largest MVPD in the world with Star, Sky, Sky Italia, and DirecTV. With Fox as a co-owner, Peter also launched Hulu.','Santa Monica, California','2023-05-02T22:25:32.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Peter Fenton','General Partner','Benchmark Capital',array['$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M','$10M - $50M','$500K - $1M']::text[],array['BioTech','Cloud Infrastructure','Consumer','Enterprise','Media/Content','AI','Developer Tools','Marketplaces']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Series B+']::text[],true,'Docker; Sorare; Cockroach Labs; Airtable; Digits; Wildlife Studios; Robocorp; Timescale',null,array['US/Canada']::text[],'http://www.twitter.com/peterfenton','https://www.linkedin.com/in/peter-fenton-0b117/','After career exits like Elastic, Twitter and Yelp, Peter Fenton is now the longest-serving full-time partner at venture capital firm Benchmark. The trained helicopter pilot more recently joined the boards of Brazil-based mobile game maker Wildlife Studios, fintech startup Digits and open-source robotic process automation provider Robocorp.','Palo Alto, California','2023-04-21T00:16:39.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Peter Goldberg','Founder and Partner','PLG Ventures',array['$0 - $100K','$100K - $500K','$500K - $1M']::text[],'{}',array['Seed','Pre-seed']::text[],true,null,null,array['USA']::text[],null,null,'Peter Goldberg is the founder of PLG Ventures based in Santa Monica.  Since 2015, Peter has been one of the most active early stage investors in SoCal. In addition, he can been seen regularly as the host of the #1 digital business show Entrepreneur Elevator Pitch. Prior to PLG, Peter held various executive positions in the banking industry including being the president and CEO of AmTrust Bank and its holding company which included the insurance and securities/brokerage divisions.','Santa Monica, California','2023-05-02T22:22:27.000Z'::timestamptz),
