('Rachel Star','Principal','Unusual Ventures',array['$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M']::text[],array['Consumer','B2C/E-Commerce','Future of Work','Productivity','B2B SaaS','Social Media','Enterprise','FinTech','Marketplaces','Direct-to-Consumer (DTC)']::text[],array['Seed','Pre-seed','Series A']::text[],false,'AltoIRA; Contra','rachel@unusual.vc',array['US/Canada']::text[],'https://twitter.com/rachel_a_star','https://www.linkedin.com/in/rachel-star-2948b288/','Rachel is Principal at Unusual helping to build and support the firm’s consumer investments. Rachel’s passion for business lies at the intersection of products and people. Rachel started her career as a consultant with McKinsey & Company with a focus on consumer brands, retailers, supply chain, and manufacturing. She then joined the Corporate Strategy team at Nordstrom Inc. Most recently, Rachel was an early-stage investor on the consumer team at Shasta Ventures. Rachel grew up in the San Francisco Bay Area, a place that has given her a deep appreciation for the entrepreneurial journey. She was a part of the team that launched SparkTruck, a non-profit organization that brought design-thinking curriculum to students across the country via a mobile classroom. She has been a speaker at TED events, for the Aspen Institute, and at Autodesk University. Rachel holds a BS from Northwestern University where she studied Manufacturing Engineering and Psychology.','San Francisco, California','2023-04-29T10:25:19.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Rafeh Saleh','General Partner','Cubit Ventures',array['$100K - $500K']::text[],array['AI','Analytics','API','AR/VR','Automation','Climate','Cloud','Consumer','DeepTech','Developer Tools','B2C/E-Commerce','Education','Enterprise','Entertainment','Future of Work','Health and Wellness','Healthcare/Medtech','Industrial','InsureTech','IoT','Life Sciences','Media','Productivity','Proptech','Robotics','B2B SaaS','Social Media','BioTech','FinTech','Marketplaces','Gaming/eSports']::text[],array['Seed']::text[],false,'Block TV; Borrow-a-boat; e-mute; feedr; go.movegb; Doorsteps.co.uk; Expert Dojo; gethoncho.co.uk; HUUB; T fitness','rafeh@cubit.vc',array['Middle East','North Africa']::text[],null,'https://www.linkedin.com/in/rafehsaleh/','Rafeh launched Cubit Ventures and Founder Institute Egypt, sits on Falak Startups board, is an advisor to Egypt Ventures and Loyal VC, and led one of the largest consulting firms in Egypt. He is an experienced triple-digit track record executive, entrepreneur, and management consultant where he advised numerous companies of all sizes on growth, turnaround, and business restructuring strategies.','Egypt','2023-04-21T05:38:30.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Rahil Rangwala','Managing Partner','Accion Venture Lab',array['$500K - $1M']::text[],array['FinTech']::text[],array['Pre-seed','Seed','Series A']::text[],true,null,'rrangwala@accion.org',array['Africa','USA','Latin America','India','Asia-Pacific','Europe','Canada','MENA']::text[],'https://twitter.com/rahil_r','https://www.linkedin.com/in/rahil-rangwala-21bb851/','Rahil is responsible for the overall strategy and success of the investment portfolio. Prior to Accion, Rahil was a Director at the Michael & Susan Dell Foundation, where he was responsible for running the India office and defining the strategic direction of (and executing against) the foundation’s Livelihoods and Financial Inclusion portfolio involving equity, debt (AUM of $70M) and grants which impacted ~7M households and ~3M youth annually. He led the Foundation’s global investment committee, where he worked closely with the program teams on the diligence for investments in all geographies. He also represented the foundation on various boards and LP advisory committees. Rahil started his professional career at Bridgewater Associates, a global macro hedge fund. Rahil has a Bachelor’s in Computer Science from the University of Texas in Austin and a Master’s in Public Administration with a focus on International Development from New York University.','India','2023-04-30T22:47:30.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Rahul Prakash','Managing Director','NOMO Ventures',array['$500K - $1M','$100K - $500K']::text[],array['Crypto/Blockchain','Enterprise','B2B SaaS','Consumer','Data Services','IoT','SaaS','Social Networks','FinTech','SMB Software']::text[],array['Seed','Pre-seed']::text[],true,'Better Mortgage; Expensify; MeUndies; SIMULATE','rahul@coyoteridgevc.com',array['Latin America','USA','Canada']::text[],'https://twitter.com/rahulprakash','https://www.linkedin.com/in/rprakash','Rahul is a successful 3x technology entrepreneur turned venture capitalist. The last company he co-founded, MyEnergy, sold to Nest prior to Google''s $3.2B acquisition. His previous company sold to NRG Energy (NYSE:NRG) for $120MM. His first venture backed company, Spock, sold to Intelius in 2009. In 2013, he founded NOMO Ventures, a venture capital fund with $115 million in assets under management. In a previous life, he served as a Press Secretary to a number of city & statewide elected officials and also had a stint in the music industry with Columbia/RuffHouse Records. He also loves hip hop, hoops, and single malt.','San Francisco Bay','2023-04-30T22:42:45.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Raj Ganguly','Co-Founder, Co-CEO & Partner','B Capital',array['$100K - $500K','$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M','$10M - $50M']::text[],array['BioTech','Enterprise','FinTech','Health IT','Consumer','TransportationTech','Generalist','Digital Health','Logistics']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Series B+']::text[],true,'Icertis; Atomwise; Evidation Health; Journera; SilverCloud Health; INTURN; Silvercar; Surf Air',null,array['USA','Canada','Asia-Pacific','India','Latin America','Europe','Africa','Israel','Australia/New Zealand','MENA']::text[],'https://twitter.com/rajganguly_','https://www.linkedin.com/in/rajganguly/','Raj''s focus is connecting extraordinary entrepreneurs with the people, capital and support needed to drive exponential growth. He is a Senior Advisor to BCG, a strategic partner to B Capital that provides a unique value-add to founders in each stage of the investment lifecycle. Raj previously was at Bain Capital investing in technology-driven companies across the U.S. and Asia. He also served as the co-leader of the firm’s global technology initiative. Earlier in his career, Raj worked at McKinsey & Company, Diageo plc and Miradiant, one of the first internet payment startups (acquired by J.P. Morgan). Raj earned an MBA from Harvard Business School, and a BSE and BAS with summa cum laude honors from the University of Pennsylvania’s Wharton School and School of Engineering and Applied Science.','Los Angeles, California','2023-04-30T22:35:48.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Raju Rishi','General Partner','RRE Ventures',array['$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M','$10M - $50M']::text[],array['Consumer','DeepTech','FinTech','CPG/D2C','Hardware','Enterprise','Proptech','Climate','Web3']::text[],array['Seed','Series A']::text[],true,'DataDog','raju@rre.com',array['USA']::text[],'https://twitter.com/rajurishi','https://www.linkedin.com/in/rajurishi/','Raju invests in passionate and tenacious entrepreneurs that are building category-defining businesses. He has a predilection for companies with deeper technology stacks, but always prioritizes exceptional teams over exceptional technology. His current areas of focus include Enterprise Technology, Healthcare IT, and Proptech. He prefers to invest at the Series A or Seed stage of a business, but doesn’t rule out later stage companies. Raju looks for startups that are disrupting massive markets, are utilizing game-changing technology, and are solving complex and meaningful problems. Before joining RRE Ventures, Raju was a Venture Partner at Sigma Prime Ventures in Boston. Most of his career, however, was spent as an entrepreneur and operator. He was the founder of several startups in the mobile and enterprise software sectors.','New York, New York','2023-04-30T22:12:16.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Rak Garg','Principal','Bain Capital Ventures',array['$3M - $10M','$10M - $50M','$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M']::text[],array['Generalist','AI','Developer Tools','B2C/E-Commerce','Enterprise','FinTech']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Series B+']::text[],true,'Tecton','rgarg@baincapital.com',array['US/Canada']::text[],'https://twitter.com/rak_garg','https://www.linkedin.com/in/rakgarg/','Rak was previously at Atlassian, where he led strategic partnerships with CASBs and shipped foundational infrastructure like IP allowlisting, a centralized logging platform, a unified admin API, and admin insights, which helped the largest companies transition pockets of PLG usage to wall-to-wall deployments. He likes working with founders who are convicted in their belief of the future while being reflective on their blind spots.','San Francisco, California','2023-04-29T10:21:09.000Z'::timestamptz),
