('Ramy Adeeb','General Partner','1984 Ventures',array['$500K - $1M']::text[],array['Digital Health','Enterprise','AI','Developer Tools','FinTech','Logistics','Proptech','Marketplaces','Consumer']::text[],array['Seed','Pre-seed']::text[],true,null,null,array['USA','Europe','Latin America']::text[],'https://twitter.com/ramyadeeb','https://www.linkedin.com/in/ramyadeeb/','An entrepreneur and investor, Ramy is founder and CEO of Snip.it (Acquired by Yahoo, where he served as a product executive) and one of the earliest engineers at Tellme Networks (Acquired by Microsoft). Ramy started his investing career at Khosla Venture where he worked with investors Vinod Khosla and Pierre Lamond on many investments including Groupme (acquired by Skype), Square (NASDAQ:SQ), and Storify (acquired by LiveFyre). He holds a BA and MS in Computer Science from Harvard and an MBA from Stanford.','San Francisco, California','2023-04-30T21:44:23.000Z'::timestamptz),
