('Ray Lane','Managing Partner','GreatPoint Ventures',array['$100K - $500K','$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M']::text[],array['CPG/D2C','Enterprise','Digital Health','BioTech','Proptech','Logistics','FinTech','Climate','Food & Ag']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Pre-seed','Series B+']::text[],true,null,null,array['USA']::text[],null,'https://www.linkedin.com/in/ray-lane-81434a15a/','Ray is a technology executive and venture capitalist best known for leading the turnaround of Oracle Corporation in the 1990’s. As Oracle’s President and COO, Ray re-established the company’s leadership in the database market and grew Oracle’s market cap by 65x to over $200 billion. After leaving Oracle, Ray became a Managing Partner with Kleiner Perkins for 14 years before becoming Partner Emeritus with the firm. Earlier in his career, Ray was a senior partner of Booz Allen Hamilton, a consulting company, and a division vice president with Electronic Data Systems Corporation. Ray currently serves on the boards of Carnegie Mellon University, Special Olympics International, and HPE. He was Executive Chairman of HP from 2011 to 2013 and Chairman of Carnegie Mellon University’s Board of Trustees from 2009 to 2015.','San Francisco, California','2023-04-30T19:24:33.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Raymond Tonsing','General Partner','Caffeinated Capital',array['$100K - $500K']::text[],array['AI','API','Automation','Climate','Cloud','Consumer','Crypto/Blockchain','DeepTech','Developer Tools','B2C/E-Commerce','Enterprise','Life Sciences','Productivity','Proptech','Robotics','B2B SaaS','Social Media','Cloud Infrastructure','Data Services','Future of Work','IoT','SaaS','BioTech','FinTech','Marketplaces']::text[],array['Multi-stage','Seed','Series A','Series B+']::text[],false,'Affirm; Airtable; Boom Supersonic; Brex; Divvy Homes; dYdX; Mighty; Opendoor; Varda Space; Virta Health; AgentSync; CloudTrucks; Varda; Playco; CryptoKitties; Voicea','rt@caffeinatedcapital.com',array['Africa','Middle East','North Africa','Oceania','Europe','Latin America','US/Canada','Asia-Pacific']::text[],'https://twitter.com/tonsing','https://www.linkedin.com/in/tonsing/','Raymond Tonsing is a San Francisco based technology investor and entrepreneur. He is the founder and managing partner of Caffeinated Capital, a technology investment firm with a portfolio that includes Affirm, Airtable, Brex, Color, dYdX, Opendoor, Virta, and Wish. Previously, Mr. Tonsing was a partner at Akkadian Ventures, a secondary fund focused on providing liquidity to founders, early employees, and angel investors of private, high-growth technology companies. Before that, Mr. Tonsing helped develop and manage Energy Central and Rigzone, two market-leading technology platforms that provide information on the energy industry. Mr. Tonsing received his B.A. from the University of Colorado, Boulder.','San Francisco, California','2023-04-21T00:16:39.000Z'::timestamptz),
