('Ryan Morgan','Managing Director','Crossbeam Venture Partners',array['$1M - $3M']::text[],array['FinTech','Enterprise','B2C/E-Commerce','Consumer','Proptech','Future of Work']::text[],array['Seed','Pre-seed']::text[],true,null,null,array['USA','Latin America','Europe']::text[],'https://twitter.com/ryan_____morgan?lang=en','https://www.linkedin.com/in/ryan-j-morgan/','Ryan is a Managing Director at Crossbeam and focuses across a variety of sectors including consumer technology, fintech, and enterprise SaaS. Prior to Crossbeam he was the co-founder of rmdy, a consumer wellness company and an active angel investor. From 2015-2018 he was on the investing team at DFJ Growth, where he helped work on their investments in Unity Technologies, SpaceX, Katerra, Outreach.io, and Ring. He has an MBA and bachelor''s degree from Wharton at the University of Pennsylvania.','United States','2023-04-28T22:17:42.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Ryan Orley','Managing Partner','Zigg Capital',array['$3M - $10M']::text[],array['Consumer','Enterprise','Proptech','B2C/E-Commerce','FinTech','AI','Developer Tools','Climate']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Pre-seed']::text[],true,null,null,array['USA','Latin America','Africa','India','Asia-Pacific','Europe','Canada','Israel','Australia/New Zealand','MENA']::text[],'https://twitter.com/ryanorley','https://www.linkedin.com/in/ryan-orley-9b63b854/','experienced investor (ex-Morgan Stanley; ex-King Street Capital)','New York, New York','2023-04-28T22:14:01.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Saam Motamedi','General Partner','Greylock',array['$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M','$10M - $50M','$50M+','$500K - $1M']::text[],array['AI','Cloud Infrastructure','Data Services','IoT','SaaS','Security','Developer Tools','Consumer','Enterprise','Web3','Cybersecurity','FinTech','Marketplaces']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Series B+']::text[],true,'apiiro; Snorkel AI; Utmost; Abnormal Security; Cresta','smotamedi@greylock.com',array['US/Canada']::text[],'https://twitter.com/saammotamedi','https://www.linkedin.com/in/saammotamedi','He partners with entrepreneurs at the seed and early stages who are focused on new opportunities in applied AI, cybersecurity, data and machine learning infrastructure, and SaaS. At Greylock, Saam has led investments in and sits on the board of security companies, and others in stealth; application companies; data & analytics companies, and infrastructure companies that are also still operating in stealth.','San Francisco, California','2023-04-21T00:16:39.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Saar Gur','General Partner','CRV',array['$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M','$10M - $50M']::text[],array['Consumer','B2B SaaS','Education','Media/Content','Real Estate','Retail','SaaS','SMB Software','Travel','Marketplaces','TransportationTech','AI','Developer Tools','Web3','BioTech','Enterprise','B2C/E-Commerce']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Series B+','Pre-seed']::text[],true,'Classpass; DoorDash; Mercury; Patreon; Ring; Office Hours; Mercury Technologies; Uppercase; Bird; Pared; Curtsy; Patreon ; Jeeves',null,array['USA','Canada']::text[],'https://twitter.com/saarsaar','https://www.linkedin.com/in/saargur/','Saar is a General Partner at CRV and was recently highlighted as #34 in the Forbes Midas List of the World’s Best Venture Capital Investors In 2021. Saar loves products that consumers and customers LOVE (over the moon LOVE), and is passionate about helping his companies succeed. He has been involved at the seed/Series A in companies like Doordash, Patreon, Ring, Classpass, Mercury and others. Saar has also been involved in over 20 acquisitions in the past few years by firms such as Google, Facebook, Apple, Disney, Rakuten and Intuit. Prior to CRV, Saar was a co-founder of BrightRoll, a leading video ad platform acquired by Yahoo for $640m in cash. He has a Stanford MBA, a biochem degree from University of Wisconsin and loves to kitesurf.','San Francisco, California','2023-04-28T21:57:23.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Sakib Jamal','Senior Associate','Crossbeam Venture Partners',array['$1M - $3M']::text[],array['FinTech','Enterprise','B2C/E-Commerce','Consumer','Proptech','Future of Work']::text[],array['Seed','Pre-seed']::text[],true,null,null,array['USA','Latin America','Europe']::text[],'https://twitter.com/skbjml','https://www.linkedin.com/in/sakibjamal/','Sakib is a member of the Investment Team and serves as a Board Observer for seven different companies in the portfolio. Prior to Crossbeam, he was an investment banking analyst at J.P. Morgan. Sakib also founded The Capsule, a South Asian news aggregator / podcast that has over 23,000 subscribers across Instagram and email. Sakib received a B.S. from Cornell University, where he served as a teaching assistant for classes in Entrepreneurship and Equity Research.','New York, New York','2023-04-28T21:01:26.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Salman Ullah','Founding Partner & Angel Investor','Merus Capital',array['$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M']::text[],array['Generalist','AI','Developer Tools','Enterprise']::text[],array['Seed','Series A']::text[],true,null,'salman@meruscap.com',array['USA']::text[],null,'https://www.linkedin.com/in/salman-ullah-6799755/','Founding Partner of Merus Capital. Previously Vice President of Corp-Dev at Google, and a General Manager for Corporate Strategy at Microsoft.','Menlo Park, California','2023-04-28T20:46:01.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Sam Altman','Angel Investor, Co-Founder & Partner','OpenAI Startup Fund; Hydrazine
  Capital',array['$0 - $25K','$25K - $100K','$100K - $500K']::text[],array['AI','Developer Tools']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Series B+','Pre-seed']::text[],true,'Routable; Humane; ANA Therapeutics; Atmos; Ashvattha Therapeutics; TrueNorth; Aspen Neuroscience; 1910 Genetics; SingleStore; Gusto; Asana; Cruise; Patreon; PlanGrid; Starsky Robotics','sam@ycombinator.com',array['USA']::text[],'http://www.twitter.com/sama',null,'For years Sam Altman has been one of the most prominent seed investors. He’s perhaps best known for his five years as the president of the famous startup accelerator Y Combinator, a role he left in 2019. Altman’s keen eye for investments helped him jump 80 spots up to No. 13 on this year’s Seed 100 list. One example: After first backing the fusion-energy startup Helion Energy in 2015, he invested $375 million in the startup''s $500 million Series E round in November, which boosted its valuation to $3 billion. When not investing, he leads OpenAI, an organization that works with open-source artificial intelligence.','San Francisco, California','2023-05-05T16:46:09.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Sam Campbell','Operations Manager','Samsung Next',array['$100K - $500K']::text[],array['AI','Cloud','Creator Economy','Crypto/Blockchain','Entertainment','Health and Wellness','Healthcare/Medtech','Robotics','FinTech','Gaming/eSports']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Series B+']::text[],false,'Alchemy; AST & Science (public); Covariant; Dapper Labs; Forte','s.campbell@samsungnext.com',array['US/Canada','Asia-Pacific']::text[],null,null,'Sam is an investor at Samsung Next, an early-stage corporate venture arm of Samsung Electronics, where he focuses on crypto & fintech companies. Prior to joining Next, Sam was managing direct venture investments for Stanford University. Sam has actively partnered with companies at the earliest stages, including jumping in part-time to build in the trenches with founders. Sam resides in the SF Bay Area with his growing family.',null,'2023-04-21T05:38:30.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Sam Englebardt','Angel Investor, Co-Founder and General Partner','Galaxy Interactive',array['$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M','$10M - $50M']::text[],array['SMB Software','AgTech','BioTech','Consumer','FinTech','Gaming/eSports','AR/VR']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Series B+']::text[],true,null,'sam@lambertmediagroup.com',array['USA']::text[],'https://www.twitter.com/samenglebardt','https://www.linkedin.com/in/samenglebardt/','Sam Englebardt is a Co-founder and Partner at Galaxy Digital and the Founding General Partner of Galaxy Interactive. He is a media and technology investor and content producer who has created, acquired and/or financed a broad range of traditional and digital businesses and dozens of films and television shows over the past decade. Prior to Galaxy Digital, Englebardt was a Partner and Managing Director at Lambert Media Group (LMG) from 2007 2016, where he sourced and managed a portfolio of media-sector private equity investments. Before LMG, Englebardt was a Vice President and Financial Advisor at Alliance Bernstein.','Los Angeles, California','2023-05-05T16:46:05.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Sam Lessin','General Partner','Slow Ventures',array['$0 - $100K','$100K - $500K','$500K - $1M']::text[],array['Enterprise','Generalist','Web3','Consumer','FinTech']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Pre-seed']::text[],true,'Identiq; OpenPhone; Fractal; Stream Club; Anomalie; Alpine Start Foods; Prefer; MasterClass; Venmo',null,array['USA']::text[],'https://twitter.com/lessin','https://www.linkedin.com/in/wlessin/','Sam is currently the co-CEO of Fin and a General Partner at Slow Ventures. He was formerly a vice president of product management at Facebook from 2010 to 2014, where he managed the People, Places, and Things product group and the Identity product group. Prior to joining Facebook Sam founded drop.io, a file-sharing platform that was acquired byFacebook in 2010. Before drop.io Sam was an associate at Bain and Company. In his spare time Sam enjoys skiing and kite-surfing. He writes a column at The Information, where he interns.','Menlo Park, California','2023-04-28T20:10:43.000Z'::timestamptz);

