('Sameer Dholakia','Partner','Bessemer Venture Partners; SendGrid',array['$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M','$10M - $50M']::text[],array['AI','Developer Tools','Cybersecurity','BioTech','Digital Health','Consumer','FinTech']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Series B+']::text[],true,'Jasper AI; Reprise','sameer.dholakia@sendgrid.com',array['USA','Canada','Israel','Asia-Pacific','Europe']::text[],null,'https://www.linkedin.com/in/sameerdholakia/','Sameer Dholakia is a partner of the growth investment practice at Bessemer. Sameer joined SendGrid as CEO and board member in 2014 to accelerate the company’s growth. He led SendGrid through a successful IPO in 2017 and subsequent acquisition by leading cloud communications platform Twilio for approximately $3 billion in early 2019. Before joining SendGrid, Sameer served as group vice president and general manager of cloud platforms group for Citrix Systems, where he was responsible for the company’s rapidly growing cloud business. He joined Citrix following its acquisition of VMLogix, where he served as CEO.','San Francisco, California','2023-04-28T17:30:52.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Sameer Gandhi','Partner','Accel',array['$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M','$10M - $50M','$500K - $1M']::text[],array['Cloud Infrastructure','Consumer Health','Consumer','Media/Content','SaaS','SMB Software','Generalist','AI','Developer Tools','Cybersecurity','Enterprise','FinTech','Digital Health','B2C/E-Commerce']::text[],array['Series A','Series B+','Seed']::text[],true,'Public.com; DecisionLink; Eagle Eye Networks; Deserve; CrowdStrike; Raise; Birchbox; Visto; Aura; Dropbox; Flipkart; Spotify; Bonobos; Diapers.com; Wonder; Trulia',null,array['US/Canada','Africa','Latin America','India','Asia-Pacific','Europe','Israel','Australia/New Zealand','Middle East','North Africa']::text[],'https://twitter.com/skg_accel','https://www.linkedin.com/in/skgandhi/','Sameer joined Accel in 2008 and focuses on consumer, cloud/saas, and media companies. Sameer is responsible for Accel''s investments in Aura, Bonobos (acquired by Walmart), CrowdStrike (CRWD), DecisionLink, Diapers.com (acquired by Amazon), DJI, Donut, Dropbox (DBX), Dropcam (acquired by Google), Eagle Eye Networks, Flipkart (acquired by Walmart), Freshworks (FRSH), Jet (acquired by Walmart), Orum, Plex (Acquired by Rockwell Automation), Public, Sonatype (acquired by Vista), Spotify (SPOT), Venmo (acquired by Braintree/PayPal), Wonder, and World View.','San Francisco, California','2023-04-20T23:35:58.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Samir Kaul','Founding General Partner','Khosla Ventures',array['$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M','$10M - $50M']::text[],array['BioTech','CleanTech/Environment','Enterprise','Food and Beverage','Health IT','DeepTech','Digital Health']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Series B+']::text[],true,'Bionaut Labs; Statespace; Siolta Therapeutics; IgGenix; Yes Health; Impossible Foods; Lightship; SWORD Health','sk@khoslaventures.com',array['USA']::text[],'https://twitter.com/samirkaul1','https://www.linkedin.com/in/samir-kaul-9227b64/','Samir focuses on health, sustainability, food, and advanced technology investments. Samir led the firm’s investments in Cadre, Guardant Health (NASDAQ: GH), Impossible Foods, Mojo Vision, NanoH2O (acquired by LG Chem), Nutanix (NASDAQ: NTNX), Oscar, Quantumscape, and Ultima,among others. Prior to co-founding Khosla Ventures, Samir spent five years at Flagship Ventures where he started and invested in early-stage biotechnology companies. While there, he was involved in co-founding Helicos BioSciences (IPO), a leader in developing single-molecule sequencing instruments to revolutionize personalized medicine, along with Stan Lapidus and Steve Quake of Stanford. Samir was also founding CEO of Codon Devices, where he raised their Series A financing, built the technical and advisory teams, and booked significant revenues in the company’s first year of operations. His other investments include Epitome (acquired by Millipore), LS9 (acquired by REG), and Morphotek (acquired by Eisai).','Menlo Park, California','2023-04-28T17:28:42.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Samit Kalra','Partner','1984 Ventures',array['$500K - $1M']::text[],array['B2C/E-Commerce','Enterprise','Healthcare/Medtech','Productivity','Proptech','B2B SaaS','FinTech','Marketplaces']::text[],array['Seed']::text[],false,'Pipe; Posthog; Sorare','samit@1984.vc',array['Europe','Latin America','US/Canada']::text[],null,'https://www.linkedin.com/in/samit-kalra-a6179365/','Samit is a partner at 1984 Ventures, a seed fund focused on software upending antiquated industries. Prior to joining 1984, Samit was a VC at Bain Capital Ventures, focusing on B2B companies at seed and Series A. Before joining Bain, Samit spent time as an operator at AngelList, helping them grow their fundraising business (syndicates and funds).','San Francisco Bay','2023-04-21T00:16:39.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Samuel Bjork','Partner','Digitalis
  Ventures',array['$0 - $100K','$100K - $500K','$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M']::text[],array['BioTech','Digital Health']::text[],array['Seed','Pre-seed','Series A','Series B+']::text[],true,null,null,array['Europe','USA']::text[],null,'https://www.linkedin.com/in/samuel-bjork-04438619/','ex-member of the healthcare and clean energy practices at the Boston Consulting Group. received graduate degrees from Cambridge and Oxford University as a Marshall Scholar and an A.B. in Chemistry from Harvard University.','Brooklyn, New York','2023-05-01T03:14:17.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Sandeep Bhadra','General Partner','Vertex Ventures',array['$0 - $100K','$100K - $500K','$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M','$10M - $50M']::text[],array['Cloud','Developer Tools','Enterprise','Industrial','InsureTech','Robotics','B2B SaaS','AI','Cloud Infrastructure','Insurance','Manufacturing','SaaS','Consumer Non-Durables','SMB Software','FinTech']::text[],array['Seed','Pre-seed','Series A','Series B+']::text[],true,'Gitpod; Hasura; Platform9; Signifyd; Tulip; Broker; Buddha; Tulip Interfaces; Astound; Quilt Data; FR8Star','Sandeep@vertexventures.com',array['Asia-Pacific','USA','Canada','Israel','India']::text[],'https://twitter.com/bhadrasandeep','https://www.linkedin.com/in/sandeepbhadra/','Sandeep is a partner at Vertex Ventures US, a seed/Series A fund based in San Francisco and Palo Alto, investing in B2B software and services. Vertex US is part of a network of funds in Israel, SE Asia, India, and China. Vertex US focuses on cloud infrastructure software (open source, dev tools, cyber security), application software powered by data warehouses and machine learning, and vertical software in large undigitized markets like finance, insurance, manufacturing and construction. Prior to Vertex, Sandeep was a principal at Menlo Ventures where he led investments in Platform9, Signifyd, Clarifai, Okera, Unravel Data. At Vertex, he works with the founders at Tulip, Hasura, LeaseLock, BrokerBuddha, Gitpod and others.','Santa Clara, California','2023-04-28T17:13:23.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Sandhya Hegde','General Partner','Unusual Ventures',array['$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M','$0 - $100K','$100K - $500K']::text[],array['Data Services','Enterprise','SaaS','Consumer','FinTech']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Pre-seed','Series B+']::text[],true,'BBOXX',null,array['USA']::text[],'https://twitter.com/sandhya','https://www.linkedin.com/in/sandhyahegde/','Sandhya Hegde is a General Partner at Unusual Ventures, leading investments in enterprise SaaS companies. She loves working with technical founders who care deeply about design and data. She aims to partner closely with CEOs to build generational businesses that raise the bar for customer and employee experience. Prior to Unusual, she was an early employee and executive at Amplitude, leading pivotal efforts across product development, category creation, fundraising and GTM strategy. As the EVP of Marketing & Growth, she helped establish Amplitude as a category leader in product analytics and the digital optimization space, overseeing 50x growth in its ARR. While at Amplitude, Sandhya also founded Amplify, the world''s leading product-led growth (PLG) conference and served as a product strategy advisor to leading startups and Fortune 100 businesses including NBC, T-Mobile and Ford.','San Francisco Bay','2023-04-28T04:12:59.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Sandhya Venkatachalam','Partner','Khosla Ventures',array['$100K - $500K','$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M','$10M - $50M']::text[],array['AI','Enterprise','Consumer','BioTech','DeepTech','Digital Health']::text[],array['Pre-seed','Seed','Series A','Series B+']::text[],true,'Forethought','sv@khoslaventures.com',array['US/Canada','Europe']::text[],'https://twitter.com/SVenkatachalam','https://www.linkedin.com/in/sandhyavenkatachalam/','Sandhya is passionate about helping founders transform industries through the use of AI/ML and other new, emerging technologies. Sandhya was previously the founder and Managing Partner of Deep Ventures, a seed investment firm focused on entrepreneurs who were tackling hard, unsolved problems through the use of AI/ML. Prior to Deep Ventures, Sandhya was a General Partner at Social Capital, co-head of the Growth Fund and the lead for AI investments. Sandhya was also the Head of Corporate Development and Vice President of Product at Skype, reporting to the CEO, post the spinout from eBay. Sandhya led the team that built an entirely new Advertising product business for Skype from pre-revenue to $100m that laid the foundation for the company’s planned IPO and eventual sale to Microsoft for $8.5 billion.','San Francisco, California','2023-04-28T04:08:50.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Sangu Delle','Executive Chairman','Golden Palm Investments',array['$0 - $100K','$100K - $500K','$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M']::text[],array['Food & Ag','Proptech','Enterprise']::text[],array['Pre-seed','Seed','Series A']::text[],true,null,null,array['Africa']::text[],'https://twitter.com/SanguDelle','https://www.linkedin.com/in/sdelle/','Currently the CEO of Africa Health Holdings Ltd. Experienced investor with a focus on healthcare.','New York, New York','2023-04-28T03:58:46.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Santiago Zavala','Managing Partner, 500 Global LatAm','500 Global',array['$0 - $100K','$100K - $500K','$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M']::text[],array['Advertising','Gaming/eSports','Media/Content','Payments','SaaS','Social Commerce','Social Networks','Generalist','Enterprise']::text[],array['Seed','Pre-seed','Series A']::text[],true,'Come Bien; doc-doc; Atexto',null,array['USA','India','Asia-Pacific','Latin America','MENA','Europe','Canada','Africa']::text[],'https://twitter.com/dfect','https://www.linkedin.com/in/santiago-zavala-47a68b7/','To date, he has made over 130 investments as part of the 500 Global family and is an expert in Product Development. He is the Founder of Mexican.VC, Super Happy Dev House Mexico City, and Startup Weekend Mexico City. Santiago is a passionate hacker and thinker who hosts his own podcast and vlog, and is also an avid photographer.','Mexico City, Mexico','2023-04-28T03:48:20.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Santo Politi','Founder and General Partner','Spark Capital',array['$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M','$10M - $50M','$0 - $100K','$100K - $500K','$500K - $1M']::text[],array['Cloud Infrastructure','Enterprise','Media/Content','Retail','DeepTech','Consumer','AI','Developer Tools','Marketplaces','FinTech','Web3']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Series B+']::text[],true,'Verana Networks; Superpedestrian; Plaid; PreVeil; Behalf; Pixie Technology; Colu; MightyTV',null,array['USA']::text[],'https://twitter.com/santopoliti','https://www.linkedin.com/in/santopoliti/','Santo started Spark in 2005 with Todd Dagres and Bijan Sabet. Prior to Spark, Santo joined Bankers Trust, to help launch the bank’s first early stage venture arm, became the President of Blockbuster, and became a general partner at Charles River Ventures.','Boston, Massachusetts','2023-04-28T03:44:42.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Sara Choi','Partner','Wing VC',array['$100K - $500K','$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M','$10M - $50M']::text[],array['Enterprise','Healthcare/Medtech','Life Sciences','AI','Analytics','Health & Hospital Services','BioTech','Developer Tools','Web3','Digital Health','Cybersecurity']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Pre-seed','Series B+']::text[],true,'Angle Health; Asimov; Jellyfish','sara@wing.vc',array['USA','Canada']::text[],'https://twitter.com/sarachoi_','https://www.linkedin.com/in/sarachoi09','Sara Choi is a Partner at Wing where she invests in companies at the intersection of bio x data. Sara enjoys working with early-stage founders half of her 12 investments are in stealth mode and bringing her background in data to healthcare and the life sciences. Sara was co-founder and COO at Airfox, a mobile data platform which was acquired by ViaVarejo (BSP: VVAR3). Prior to founding Airfox, Sara was Head of Product at Ciao Telecom where she co-founded a new wireless carrier. Sara began her career at Google where she led teams as YouTube’s Media Lead and Product Marketing Lead for Google Partners.','San Francisco Bay','2023-04-28T01:48:55.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Sarah Catanzaro','General Partner','Amplify Partners',array['$100K - $500K','$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M']::text[],array['AI','Cloud Infrastructure','Data Services','Enterprise','Developer Tools','Cybersecurity']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Series B+']::text[],true,'Runway; Hex.tech; OctoML','sarah@amplifypartners.com',array['US/Canada']::text[],'https://twitter.com/sarahcat21','https://www.linkedin.com/in/sarah-catanzaro-9770b98/','Focuses on startups that apply technological advances in machine intelligence and enterprise infrastructure to solve real-world problems. In her first position as a Research Director for the Center for Advanced Defense Studies (CADS), Sarah and her team used advanced statistical models to predict the behavior of covert organizations, including Somali pirates, illicit charcoal traders, and jihadist insurgencies. She subsequently leveraged computational methods to help public agencies ranging from the US Joint Forces Command to the Secret Service anticipate and disrupt complex threats. Upon joining Mattermark as Head of Data, she applied similar approaches to incomplete and uncertain datasets on private companies. Sarah started her career in venture capital at Canvas Ventures, where she utilized similar methodologies to source the firm’s investments in Fluxx, Platform9, and Kinetica.','San Francisco, California','2023-04-14T23:35:36.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Sarah Fox','Associate','Windham
