('Steve Vassallo','General Partner','Foundation Capital',array['$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M']::text[],array['CleanTech/Environment','Consumer','AI','Developer Tools','Enterprise','FinTech','Web3']::text[],array['Series A','Series B+','Seed']::text[],true,'Loft Orbital; ForUsAll; Runtime; Autogrid; Bolt Threads; Beepi; Sentient Energy; Pocket; Cerebras Systems; Stripe; Threads',null,array['USA']::text[],'https://www.twitter.com/vassallo?lang=en','https://www.linkedin.com/in/stevevassallo/','Steve invests at the intersection of design, technology, and business: at the sweet spot where a product meets a real user need, is built atop a unique insight or technological breakthrough, and has the potential to be a massive business. He is drawn to founders with two predilections: First, having spent the initial five years of his career designing products at IDEO, Steve gravitates towards product-first founders, who understand how to build technology that delights and improves the lives of its users. Second, he is drawn to founders who want to solve consequential problems. Steve’s investments include Anomalo, Bolt Threads, Brave, Cerebras Systems, Control4 [CTRL], Dust Labs, ForUsAll, Framer, KeeperTax, Loft Orbital, Mantle, Mode, Northstar, OAK Networks, Outerbounds, Pareto Labs, Pocket (acquired by Mozilla), Portals, PrivateCore (acquired by Facebook), Simple Habit, Stripe, Solana [SOL], Sunrun [RUN], Teleport, and Threads.','San Francisco, California','2023-04-22T21:19:14.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Steven A. Cohen','Chairman','Point72 Ventures',array['$100K - $500K','$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M','$10M - $50M']::text[],array['DeepTech','Cybersecurity','FinTech','Enterprise']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Series B+']::text[],true,null,null,array['USA']::text[],'https://twitter.com/StevenACohen2',null,'Steven A. Cohen is the Chairman and Chief Executive Officer of Point72, a 1,800+ person registered investment advisor. Mr. Cohen founded S.A.C. Capital Advisors in 1992 and converted his investment operations to the Point72 Asset Management family office in 2014. Mr. Cohen has leveraged his lengthy career in the public markets to found Point72 Ventures, a global venture capital strategy, and Point72 Hyperscale, a private equity strategy that seeks to drive value creation through applied AI.','Greenwich, Connecticut','2023-04-22T21:11:50.000Z'::timestamptz),
