('Sunil Dhaliwal','Founder and General Partner','Amplify Partners',array['$100K - $500K','$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M']::text[],array['Analytics','Cloud Infrastructure','Enterprise','SaaS','Security','AI','Developer Tools','Cybersecurity']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Series B+']::text[],true,'InterVenn; mabl; VeriSIM Life; covariant.ai; Fastly; Backtrace; Keen; Conjur; Inc.; Covariant; Hex; Runway; Sym','sunil@amplifypartners.com',array['USA']::text[],'https://twitter.com/dhaliwas','https://www.linkedin.com/in/sunildhaliwal/','Founded Amplify in 2012, returning to the list in 2020. Prior to founding Amplify Partners, Sunil was a General Partner at Battery Ventures where he spent 14 years investing in category-defining IT infrastructure companies such as Chef, Netezza (acquired by IBM), Splunk (NASDAQ: SPLK), CipherTrust (acquired by Secure Computing), and @stake (acquired by Symantec). Sunil gets tremendous energy from helping companies go from zero to one. Believing in an idea, helping it take shape, and then seeing it manifest in products, customers, and employees is magical.','San Francisco Bay','2023-04-22T15:25:08.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Sunny Dhillon','Partner','Signia Venture Partners',array['$100K - $500K','$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M']::text[],array['Advertising','Analytics','Consumer Health','Education','Hardware','MarketingTech','Media/Content','Security','SMB Software','Media','Gaming/eSports','AI','Developer Tools','Enterprise','FinTech','B2C/E-Commerce','AR/VR','Consumer','Cybersecurity']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Pre-seed','Series B+']::text[],true,'TrustToken; Harbor; Anomalie; Drifter Entertainment; Eonite Perception; 8i; Super Evil Mega Corp; Cruise','sunny@signiaventurepartners.com',array['USA']::text[],'https://twitter.com/SunDhillon','https://www.linkedin.com/in/sundhillon/','Invests across both consumer and enterprise tech, with a particular interest in content infrastructure, ecommerce, and retail tech. He serves on the boards of portfolio companies Drifter Entertainment, MomentFeed and Nativo.  He also works closely with past portfolio companies Cruise (acq. by General Motors) and Phoenix Labs (acq. by SEA Garena), and served as an observer on the boards of both Grow Mobile (acq. by Perion, Inc.) and Tenor (acq. by Google).  He was also responsible for incubating Skale Networks at Signia and leading the fund’s blockchain thesis.','San Francisco, California','2023-04-21T20:37:27.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Suraj Patel','Partner, Education','Workshop Venture Partners',array['$0 - $100K','$100K - $500K','$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M']::text[],array['EdTech','Climate']::text[],array['Seed','Pre-seed']::text[],true,null,null,array['USA']::text[],null,'https://www.linkedin.com/in/surajcpatel/','Strategy & people-leader with experience across private, public, and social sectors across a variety of functional areas: operations, strategy (development and implementation), growth, and organizational effectiveness & design. Proven people-developer. Passionate about mission-driven work, with experience in education (PK-12), global health, city government/public services, and democracy.','Santa Ana, California','2023-04-27T19:10:52.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Susan Liu','Partner','Uncork Capital',array['$3M - $10M','$10M - $50M']::text[],array['AI','Analytics','Automation','Creator Economy','B2C/E-Commerce','Enterprise','Future of Work','Productivity','Proptech','B2B SaaS','Supply Chain','Diverse Investors','Enterprise Applications','SaaS','FinTech']::text[],array['Seed','Series B+']::text[],false,'Papaya Global; WalkMe; Wrike','susan@uncorkcapital.com',array['Europe','US/Canada']::text[],'https://twitter.com/susanwliu?lang=en','https://www.linkedin.com/in/susanwliu/','Susan invests in software for enterprises, small-to-medium businesses and employees, no matter where they work: at home or in an office. She has spent a decade analyzing SaaS businesses across multiple dimensions and is constantly on the hunt for net-new ideas — products and markets that don’t yet exist, but which solve legitimate, provable problems. Prior to joining Uncork Capital in 2021, Susan spent nine years as a software investor at Scale Venture Partners, where she studied workplace trends and b2b software. Her experience in working with Series A and Series B companies means she knows what it takes for seed startups to reach the next milestone.','San Francisco, California','2023-04-20T23:03:06.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Susan Lyne','Founding Partner, President & Managing Partner; President and Managing Partner','BBG Ventures',array['$0 - $100K','$100K - $500K']::text[],array['Diverse Investors','SMB Software','Under-represented founders','B2C/E-Commerce','Digital Health','Future of Work']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Pre-seed']::text[],true,'Winky Lux; Maverick; Maven Clinic; Levo','susan.lyne@bbgv.com',array['USA']::text[],'http://twitter.com/smlyne','https://www.linkedin.com/in/slyne','Susan has held leadership positions at companies of all sizes and stages, from startups to public companies, media to eCommerce, Editor-in-Chief to CEO. Decades of learning and leading at Disney, ABC (where she greenlit shows like Desperate Housewives and Grey’s Anatomy), Martha Stewart Living Omnimedia, Gilt.com and AOL’s Brand Group reinforced a conviction that women are the key drivers of economic growth and cultural change -- and in 2014 she made the leap to launch BBG Ventures with Nisha. With four daughters, three sisters, and scores of smart women in her orbit, her biggest wins have come from listening to, building for and betting on women.','New York, New York','2023-04-21T20:32:28.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Suvir Sujan','Co-Founder and Managing Director','Nexus Venture Partners',array['$0 - $100K','$100K - $500K','$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M']::text[],array['Enterprise']::text[],array['Pre-seed','Seed','Series A']::text[],true,null,null,array['USA','India']::text[],'https://twitter.com/suvirsujan','https://www.linkedin.com/in/suvir-sujan-66023b3/','Suvir is a successful entrepreneur and pioneer of the Indian consumer internet. Suvir has been co-founder and co-CEO of Baazee.com, the leading online marketplace in India that merged with eBay in 2004 to form eBay India. Post the merger, Suvir was Country Manager, eBay India and Director, PayPal. Suvir has also worked as a Management Consultant at the Boston Consulting Group in New York and Mumbai. He began his career at Nortel Networks. Suvir has an MBA from the Harvard Business School where he was the Co-President of the South Asian Business Association and a BS in Electrical Engineering (High Distinction) from the University of Maryland at College Park. He is a charter member of the Internet and Mobile Association of India and a mentor to several entrepreneurs in the consumer services sector in India. He has also served on the board of the Global India Venture Capital Association.','India','2023-04-21T20:29:32.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Suzanne Norris','Managing Partner','Victress Capital; Visible Ventures',array['$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M']::text[],array['Under-represented founders','B2C/E-Commerce','Digital Health','EdTech','CPG/D2C']::text[],array['Seed','Series A']::text[],true,null,null,array['USA','Canada']::text[],null,'https://www.linkedin.com/in/suzannenorris/','brings a unique skill set to the Victress team with both an investment and operating background. started her career in investment banking at Robertson Stephens at the beginning of the Internet boom joined Liz Claiborne Inc where she developed e-commerce strategies and led the e-commerce businesses for 7 portfolio brands including Kate Spade. After leaving Kate Spade, Suzanne started her own consulting practice to work with smaller consumer brands that wanted to develop e-commerce strategies that aligned brand and commerce goals','Boston, Massachusetts','2023-04-21T20:24:36.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Sven Strohband','Managing Director','Khosla Ventures',array['$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M','$10M - $50M']::text[],array['AI','Robotics','SMB Software','BioTech','DeepTech','Digital Health']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Series B+']::text[],true,'Luka (dba Replika); Vicarious; Idibon','sst@khoslaventures.com',array['USA']::text[],'https://twitter.com/sstrohband','https://www.linkedin.com/in/sven-strohband-348b841/','At Khosla Ventures, Sven led the firm’s investments in Berkshire Grey, GitLab, and Rocket Lab, among others. An engineer at heart, Sven is passionate about technologies that forge new industries and enable novel user experiences. He spent six years at Mohr Davidow Ventures where he led technical diligence for the infrastructure IT and sustainability practices. He also worked with the firm’s companies, recruiting technical talent, running product-market fit experiments and crafting fundraising strategies. Previously, Sven was a project manager for the Electronics Research Lab of Volkswagen, where he led technical projects for Volkswagen brands, and also served as lead engineer and project lead for the Stanford racing team’s autonomous car, Stanley, which went on to win the 2005 DARPA Grand Challenge. Now on display at the Smithsonian Museum, Stanley became the foundation for the Google self-driving car project.','Mountain View, California','2023-04-21T20:12:55.000Z'::timestamptz),
