('Tess Hatch','Partner','Bessemer Venture Partners',array['$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M','$10M - $50M']::text[],array['AgTech','AI','AR/VR','Hardware','IoT','Manufacturing','Robotics','Space','TransportationTech','Developer Tools','Cybersecurity','BioTech','Digital Health','Consumer','FinTech']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Series B+']::text[],true,'Boom Supersonic; Atomo Coffee',null,array['USA','Canada','Israel','Asia-Pacific','Europe']::text[],null,'https://www.linkedin.com/in/tesshatch/','Tess invests in technology and people who believe as strongly as she does that frontier technology will develop solutions for societal problems. Tess earned a Bachelor’s degree in aerospace engineering from the University of Michigan and a Master’s degree in aeronautics and astronautics engineering from Stanford. She went on to work for Boeing and then SpaceX where she worked with the government on integrating its payloads with the Falcon9 rocket. She remains close to her alma mater by co-teaching a class at Stanford, serving on the board of advisors for the Stanford Technology Ventures Program, and founding the Stanford Aero/Astro Alumni Association.','San Francisco Bay','2023-04-21T09:29:02.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Theo Lee','Senior Associate','25M Health',array['$500K - $1M']::text[],array['Digital Health']::text[],array['Pre-seed','Seed','Series A','Series B+']::text[],true,null,'theo.lee@25madison.com',array['USA']::text[],'https://twitter.com/theoalee','https://www.linkedin.com/in/theoalee/','On the side Theo leads A-Level Capital, a student-run $2M fund, supporting and investing in Johns Hopkins-affiliated entrepreneurs. What excites them the most is working with passionate entrepreneurs and disruptive technology/business models that seek to make the world a more sustainable and healthy place to live.','New York, New York','2023-04-20T19:39:43.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Theresia Gouw','Founding Partner; Venture Capitalist','Acrew Capital',array['$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M','$10M - $50M']::text[],array['Healthcare/Medtech','SMB Software','AI','Diverse Investors','Enterprise','Security','Under-represented founders','Cybersecurity','FinTech']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Series B+']::text[],true,'Pacaso; Ketch; Solv; PredictHQ; Deserve; Exabeam; Cato Networks; Akorda; imperva; Trulia','theresia@aspectventures.com',array['USA','Latin America','Israel']::text[],'https://twitter.com/tgr','https://www.linkedin.com/in/theresiagouw/','Prior to co-founding Acrew Capital, Theresia was a co-founder at Aspect Ventures and a Managing General Partner at Accel. Theresia has been fortunate to work with many successful companies through IPOs or acquisitions. Theresia was named to Forbes’ 100 Most Powerful Women list, has been recognized 9 times on the Forbes Midas List, was named one of the 40 Most Influential Minds in Tech by Time Magazine, named to the Carnegie Corporation’s annual Distinguished Immigrants List, as well as being listed in 2022 Forbes 50 over 50.','San Francisco Bay','2023-04-20T23:03:06.000Z'::timestamptz),
