('Tim Draper','Founder & Managing Partner','Draper Associates; Hero City at Draper University',array['$100K - $500K','$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M','$10M - $50M']::text[],array['Consumer Health','FinTech','Local Services','Media/Content','Messaging','Payments','SMB Software','Social Commerce','Travel','Marketplaces']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Series B+']::text[],true,'Robinhood',null,array['USA']::text[],'https://twitter.com/TimDraper','https://www.linkedin.com/in/timothydraper/','Tim Draper founded Draper Associates, DFJ and the Draper Venture Network, a global network of venture capital funds. He funded Baidu, Tesla, Skype, SpaceX, Twitch, Hotmail, Focus Media, Robinhood, Athenahealth, Box, Cruise Automation, Carta, Planet, PTC and 15 other unicorns at the seed stage. He is a supporter and global thoughtleader for entrepreneurs everywhere, and is a leading spokesperson for Bitcoin, Blockchain, ICOs and cryptocurrencies, invested in over 50 crypto companies, and led investments in Coinbase, Ledger, Tezos, and Bancor, among others. He has received various awards and honors including the World Entrepreneurship Forum’s “Entrepreneur of the World,” and is listed as one of the top 100 most powerful people in finance by Worth Magazine, the top 20 most influential people in Crypto by CryptoWeekly, #1 most networked VC by AlwaysOn, #7 on the Forbes Midas List, and #48 most influential Harvard Alum.','Redwood City, California','2023-04-25T16:35:28.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Tim Guleri','Managing Director','Sierra Ventures',array['$100K - $500K','$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M','$10M - $50M']::text[],array['AI','Cloud Infrastructure','Data Services','SaaS','Security','Developer Tools','Cybersecurity','Digital Health','Web3','Hardware','B2C/E-Commerce','EdTech','Enterprise','FinTech','Marketplaces']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Series B+']::text[],true,'Fabric; Balto; Phenom People; Zycada Networks; Text IQ; HeadSpin; Appcues; LeadGenius',null,array['USA']::text[],'https://twitter.com/timguleri','https://www.linkedin.com/in/timguleri/','Tim Guleri is a former serial entrepreneur, having built two successful software infrastructure companies: Scopus Technology (IPO in 1995) and Octane Software (M&A – Epiphany $3.2 billion). He joined Sierra Ventures as Managing Director in 2002 and focuses on Big Data and Artificial Intelligence. Since joining, he has taken two companies public (Sourcefire – FIRE and MakeMyTrip – MMYT), and has been responsible for several M&As.','San Francisco Bay','2023-04-21T00:16:39.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Tim Shannon','General Partner','Canaan Partners',array['$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M','$10M - $50M','$100K - $500K']::text[],array['Health IT','Pharmaceuticals','BioTech','Health & Hospital Services','Cybersecurity','Digital Health','Enterprise','AI','Developer Tools','Consumer','DeepTech','FinTech']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Series B+']::text[],true,'Rallybio; Vivace Therapeutics; IDEAYA Biosciences; NextCure; Arvinas; Spyryx Biosciences; CytomX Therapeutics; Civitas Therapeutics',null,array['USA','Africa','Latin America','India','Asia-Pacific','Europe','Canada','Israel','Australia/New Zealand','MENA']::text[],'https://twitter.com/TimShannonMD','https://www.linkedin.com/in/tim-shannon-85905328/','Tim pairs his operating experience and medical background to create value for companies from the earliest stage through FDA approval. Prior to becoming an investor, Tim began as a pulmonary and critical care physician, and was the president and chief executive officer of CuraGen, a publicly traded biopharmaceutical company focused on oncology. Tim earned his medical degree from the University of Connecticut and has a B.A. in chemistry from Amherst College.','Westport, Connecticut','2023-04-27T19:11:26.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Tim Smith','Partner','Bee
