('Yoram Oron','Founder & General Partner','Vertex Ventures',array['$100K - $500K','$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M','$0 - $100K']::text[],array['Enterprise']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Series B+']::text[],true,'Cylus; Argus Cyber Security; SolarEdge Technologies; Correlsense; Heptagon Advanced Micro Optics; Inside Secure; Waze; Wisair',null,array['USA','Asia-Pacific','Israel','India']::text[],null,'https://www.linkedin.com/in/yoram-oron-10599a/','Yoram Oron founded Vertex Ventures Israel in 1997 Yoram led investments in Cyber-Ark (NASDAQ: CYBR, $1.5B market cap), Waze (sold to Google for $1.3B), Argus (Sold to Continental for over $400M) Morecom (sold to Liberate, US$561M), and Vision Tech (sold to Broadcom, US$250M). Yoram holds an impressive track record both as a founder and manager of several successful high technology companies. Prior to founding Vertex, Yoram was a co-founder and Chairman of Telegate from its inception in 1993 until its acquisition by Terayon in 1999 for US$400 million. Previously, Yoram was President and CEO of Aryt Industries (NASDAQ: ARYTF), Co-Founder of Geotek Communications and Manager of its Military Division, and Co-Founder, President and CEO of Reshef Technologies.','Israel','2023-04-13T20:15:42.000Z'::timestamptz),
