('Zach Bratun-Glennon','Founder and Partner','Gradient Ventures',array['$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M']::text[],array['Advertising','AI','Consumer','Developer Tools','FinTech','B2C/E-Commerce']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Pre-seed']::text[],true,'Wise; Moov','zbg+external@gradient.com',array['US/Canada']::text[],null,'https://www.linkedin.com/in/zachary-bratun-glennon-b4a16026/','Prior to Gradient, Zach led acquisitions and strategic investments as a member of Google’s Corporate Development team, where he focused on Google’s Cloud, Ads and Commerce businesses. Before Google, Zach advised software and internet companies as an investment banker, leading companies through M&As, IPOs, and other financing opportunities. Zach started his career as a quant and data scientist at a leading energy trading hedge fund, and also co-founded a social media startup. Zach serves on the Board of Directors at Openly, Elsa, and Wise Systems, among other companies. He received his bachelor’s degree in Computer Science and Applied Mathematics from the University of Virginia, his JD from the UCLA School of Law, and his MBA from the UCLA Anderson School of Management.','San Francisco, California','2023-04-20T23:35:58.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Zach DeWitt','Partner','Wing VC; Wing Venture Capital',array['$100K - $500K','$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M','$10M - $50M']::text[],array['B2B SaaS','AI','Developer Tools','Web3','Digital Health','Cybersecurity','BioTech','FinTech','Marketplaces']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Pre-seed','Series B+']::text[],true,'Gong; Snowflake; Deepgram; Uber; Starkware','zach@wing.vc',array['US/Canada']::text[],'https://twitter.com/zacharydewitt','https://www.linkedin.com/in/zachary-dewitt-a5a8b816/','Zach DeWitt is a Partner at Wing. Prior to Wing, Zach was CEO and co-founder of Drop, Inc., which built two award-winning iPhone apps (Drop Messages and Firefly) before selling its technology and intellectual property to Snapchat in 2016. Before founding Drop, Zach worked in the technology, media and telecommunications groups at both TPG Capital and Goldman Sachs, where he was involved with various technology deals, including TPG''s investment in Uber. Zach holds a BA in Economics from Yale University, cum laude, and an MBA from the Harvard Business School, where he graduated as a Baker Scholar. Zach writes about the proliferation of product-led growth (PLG), highlighting the best (public + private) PLG companies in his weekly newsletter, Notorious PLG.','San Francisco, California','2023-04-21T00:16:39.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Zack Lynch','Managing Partner','Jazz Venture Partners',array['$0 - $100K','$100K - $500K','$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M']::text[],array['Enterprise','Digital Health','AI','Developer Tools','AR/VR','BioTech','Gaming/eSports']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Series B+']::text[],true,null,null,array['USA']::text[],'https://twitter.com/rallyzack','https://www.linkedin.com/in/zacklynch/','Zack is an entrepreneur and futurist who has deep insight into how emerging technologies impact industry and human society. He is a proactive board member and investor across a broad array of technology and health-related markets and enjoys helping innovators achieve their visions. Before JAZZ, Zack built several companies focused on connecting industries including a global conference ecosystem that enabled thousands of startups to tap into new sources of capital. Needing to share his vision for the next 50 years, he wrote the global best-selling book, The Neuro Revolution: How Brain Science Is Changing Our World.','San Francisco, California','2023-04-21T05:38:30.000Z'::timestamptz),
