('Zack Smotherman','Private Equity Investor & General Partner','Battery Ventures',array['$100K - $500K','$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M','$10M - $50M']::text[],array['AI','Developer Tools','Enterprise','Digital Health','B2C/E-Commerce','BioTech','Cybersecurity','DeepTech','EdTech','Proptech','FinTech']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Series B+']::text[],true,null,null,array['USA','Europe','Israel']::text[],null,'https://www.linkedin.com/in/zack-smotherman-6994983/','Zack joined the firm in 2013 and helps lead Battery’s growing industrial-technology and life science tools practice, backing later-stage, buyout investments in the U.S. and Europe. Prior to Battery, Zack was an investor at WestView Capital Partners, where he evaluated and executed middle-market buyout and recapitalization transactions across the tech-enabled services and software sectors. Zack began his career in the investment banking group at Avondale Partners.','Boston, Massachusetts','2023-04-20T23:03:06.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Zak Kukoff','Principal','General Catalyst',array['$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M','$10M - $50M']::text[],array['Digital Health','Consumer','Enterprise','Web3','FinTech']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Series B+']::text[],true,'Overjet','zkukoff@generalcatalyst.com',array['Latin America','India','US/Canada']::text[],'https://twitter.com/zck','https://www.linkedin.com/in/kukoff/','My first exposure to entrepreneurship was in high school, where I launched an ed-tech startup that I later took to Techstars Boulder. That experience taught me a few important lessons: failure teaches as much as success, the founder’s journey can be lonely, and good investors provide a lot more than money. I brought those learnings to the Dorm Room Fund at NYU, which I helped run as an undergrad. That’s where I learned about General Catalyst’s student founder program, Rough Draft Ventures. After graduation, I moved to Silicon Valley to work in operations for a high-growth logistics company. This was the opposite of lonely – the company added 500 employees during my year there. I made the transition to venture shortly after to support founders at the earliest stages of realizing their visions. I came to General Catalyst for the opportunity to partner with founders at the early stages of company building.','San Francisco, California','2023-04-20T23:03:06.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Zane Lackey','General Partner','Andreessen Horowitz',array['$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M','$10M - $50M']::text[],array['SMB Software','AI','Developer Tools','Cybersecurity','Web3','DeepTech','BioTech','Digital Health','Consumer','FinTech','AR/VR','Gaming/eSports']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Series B+']::text[],true,'Material Security; Panther Labs','zane@signalsciences.com',array['Asia-Pacific','US/Canada']::text[],'https://twitter.com/zanelackey','https://www.linkedin.com/in/zane-lackey-66a3404/','Zane was previously the cofounder and chief security officer of Signal Sciences, which was acquired by Fastly for $775 million in 2020, and the author of Building a Modern Security Program. Prior to Signal Sciences, Zane led security and infrastructure teams as the CISO of Etsy, and started his career as an early security consultant at iSEC Partners. Zane holds a BA in Economics with a minor in Computer Science from UC Davis.','New York, New York','2023-04-21T05:38:30.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Zeeza Cole','Principal','Bain Capital Ventures',array['$500K - $1M','$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M','$10M - $50M']::text[],array['Enterprise','B2B SaaS','Consumer','Generalist','AI','Developer Tools','B2C/E-Commerce','FinTech']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Series B+']::text[],true,'Archive; Disclo','zcole@baincapital.com',array['US/Canada']::text[],'https://twitter.com/ZeezaCole','https://www.linkedin.com/in/zeeza-cole-014007134/','Zeeza Cole partners with early-stage founders building the next generation of software products. At the earliest stages, she is investing in visions for what the future could look like, and the people and stories behind them. At the same time, she is focused on identifying opportunities that have the potential to fundamentally transform major industries – be it solving an entirely unmet need or restructuring an antiquated process or workflow.','San Francisco, California','2023-04-20T23:35:58.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Zia Huque','General Partner','Prime Movers Lab',array['$1M - $3M','$3M - $10M']::text[],array['BioTech']::text[],array['Seed','Series A','Series B+']::text[],true,null,null,array['USA']::text[],null,'https://www.linkedin.com/in/zia-huque-b756431b6/','Zia Huque is a General Partner of Prime Movers Lab where he focuses on growth-stage investing. Zia brings a wealth of experience in later-stage financing, having been in the business of risk investment and risk management across credit, rates, equities, and derivatives asset classes for the vast majority of his career. Zia also brings his operational expertise to Prime Movers Lab, having had vast executive, strategic and operational responsibilities across multiple businesses and regions of a top-five global investment bank managing tens of billions of dollars and thousands of employees. He led investments in Energy Vault (NRGV), Lyten, and Upward Farms. He also serves on the boards of Boom Supersonic and Vaxxinity.','Jackson, Wyoming','2023-04-27T18:48:28.000Z'::timestamptz),
('Zoe Oz','Co-Founder & CMO','Kairos HQ','{}','{}',array['Seed','Pre-seed','Series A']::text[],true,null,null,array['USA']::text[],null,'https://www.linkedin.com/in/zoeoz/','Zoe is the Chief Marketing Officer at Kairos. She leads brand and marketing strategy as well as new product development. She previously developed & led the Kairos Fellowship, a community of the brightest young entrepreneurs around the world. Prior to joining Kairos, Zoe held positions in various medical research labs, including the cardiovascular division at Columbia Presbyterian Hospital, where she conducted analyses on the effects of sleep deprivation on young medical professionals.','New York, New York','2023-04-12T19:55:04.000Z'::timestamptz);
